module engine where

-- =========================================================================
-- totality.fenel — the totality checker, RUNG 1 (structural recursion) +
-- RUNG 2 (guarded measure / well-founded descent) + RUNG 3 (slice A:
-- lexicographic descent; slice B: SIZE-CHANGE graph closure, ONE function;
-- slice C: MUTUAL recursion — the call-graph closure over a SET of functions).
-- unified-static-analysis Phase 1 (rung 1) + Phase 3a (rung 2) + Phase 3c
-- (rung 3a) + Phase 3d (rung 3b) + Phase 3e (rung 3c). Briefs:
-- `workstreams/unified-static-analysis/briefs/phase-1-analyze-skeleton-and-totality-rung1.md`,
-- `workstreams/unified-static-analysis/briefs/phase-3a-totality-rung2-measure.md`,
-- `workstreams/unified-static-analysis/briefs/phase-3c-totality-rung3-lexicographic.md`,
-- `workstreams/unified-static-analysis/briefs/phase-3d-totality-rung3-size-change-graph.md`,
-- `workstreams/unified-static-analysis/briefs/phase-3e-totality-rung3c-mutual-recursion.md`.
--
-- THE SOUNDNESS PAYLOAD. Fenel's headline is dependent types + runtime
-- proofs; a proof is a value inhabiting a proposition (Curry-Howard). Under
-- general recursion a non-terminating term inhabits ANY proposition (`loop :
-- P = loop`), so the kernel's reduction / `PropForall` rules are unsound
-- until we can certify the backing definitions TERMINATE. This module is the
-- first rung of that certificate.
--
-- RUNG 1 = STRUCTURAL RECURSION. A self-call is "decreasing" when one of its
-- arguments is a variable that is a STRUCTURAL SUB-TERM of a parameter — i.e.
-- a variable bound by destructuring (a `PatConstruct` field) of a parameter,
-- or of an already-smaller variable. A definition is `Total` at rung 1 when
-- EVERY self-call has at least one decreasing argument (and trivially when it
-- has no self-call). When some self-call is NOT structurally decreasing, rung
-- 1 returns `Unknown` (a measure / size-change argument may still prove it).
-- Provable divergence + the `@partial` escape-hatch give `Partial`; the AST
-- walk produces only `Total | Unknown`, the `@partial` flag is folded in by
-- `totalityVerdict`.
--
-- RUNG 2 = GUARDED MEASURE / WELL-FOUNDED DESCENT (Phase 3a). The canonical
-- NUMERIC recursion rung 1 misses: `f n = if n > 0 then f (n - 1) else 0`. A
-- self-call is rung-2 decreasing when an argument is `sub v 1` (`v - 1`) with
-- `v` proven `> 0` in the call's branch — the strict decrease `v-1 < v` is
-- always true, and the `v > 0` GUARD supplies well-foundedness (`v-1 ≥ 0`, so
-- the ℕ-descent is finite). The soundness crux is the guard: an UNGUARDED
-- `f (v - 1)` may underflow (`0 → -1 → -2 → …` diverges), so rung 2 returns
-- `Unknown` for it (a wrong `Total` there is the exact unsoundness totality
-- exists to prevent). NUMERIC DOMAIN (2026-10-03): `v - 1 < v` is NOT always
-- true of JS Numbers (`1e20 - 1 = 1e20`, `Infinity - 1 = Infinity`, and NaN or
-- a non-number passes every NEGATED comparison), so `pos` now holds branch FACTS
-- ({name, fact} records: "lower" v > 0, "upper" v ≤ 2^53, "number" v a non-NaN
-- Number, the last proved only by a comparison that evaluated to true) and a unit
-- decrement counts only under all three (totCanDecrement). An unbounded
-- countdown (`if n > 0 then f (n - 1)`) is Unknown; `if n > 0 && n <= 1000000`
-- proves it. The guard supplies a THIRD threaded set — `pos`, the
-- branch facts (positivity, the exact-decrement bound, Number-ness of named
-- variables) known in the current branch — established by the `if`
-- guards the walk descends through (`totPosFromCond` / `totPosFromCondNeg`,
-- narrowing re-expressed over core `Expr`). FENCE (rung-2b / rung-3): k≥2
-- decrements (`v - 2` needs `v ≥ 2`), non-`sub` measures (`div v 2`) — each
-- stays `Unknown`.
--
-- RUNG 3 (slice A) = LEXICOGRAPHIC DESCENT under a fixed (identity) parameter
-- order (Phase 3c). THE SOUNDNESS REPAIR. Rungs 1+2 decided a self-call total
-- when SOME argument decreases — a test that is POSITION-AGNOSTIC. For a
-- multi-argument function that is UNSOUND: the decrease must be credited to the
-- RIGHT position (each parameter's NEW value compared against ITS OWN old
-- value). Two counterexamples were wrongly accepted as `Total` by rungs 1+2,
-- both NON-TERMINATING:
--   • structural cross-position: `f a b = case a of Cons h t -> f (Cons h t) t`
--     (`t` lands in `b`'s slot; `a` is reconstructed — `a` never shrinks);
--   • measure cross-position: `f a b = if a > 0 then f (b + 1) (a - 1) else 0`
--     (`a-1` lands in `b`'s slot — `f 2 0 → f 1 1 → f 2 0` cycles).
-- The position-agnostic "some arg decreases" fold credited the decrease to the
-- WRONG parameter. Slice A replaces it with the POSITION-AWARE criterion: the
-- parameter tuple `(p₀ … pₙ₋₁)` strictly DECREASES in LEXICOGRAPHIC order at
-- every self-call —
--     ∃k. (∀ i < k. argᵢ ≡ pᵢ)  ∧  (arg_k ≺ p_k)
-- reading left-to-right, the FIRST position whose argument is not provably
-- EQUAL to its own parameter must be provably STRICTLY LESS than its own
-- parameter. Per position `i` (param `pᵢ`, argument `argᵢ`):
--   • RelEq  ⟺ `argᵢ = EVar pᵢ` (the same parameter, unchanged, in its slot);
--   • RelLt  ⟺ structural (`argᵢ = EVar v` with `origin(v) = pᵢ` — a strict
--             sub-term of `pᵢ`, in `pᵢ`'s slot) OR guarded measure (`argᵢ =
--             sub pᵢ 1` with `pᵢ ∈ pos`);
--   • otherwise RelUnknown (a different param's sub-term, a construction, any
--             unrecognized shape — cross-position lands HERE).
-- SOUND because the measure is the parameter tuple under lexicographic order:
-- each component's domain is well-founded (structural sizes ∈ ℕ; a guarded
-- measure stays ≥ 0 within its descent), and lex order over finitely-many
-- well-founded components is well-founded. A SINGLE fixed (identity) order must
-- work for ALL self-calls; different calls may decrease at different `k`. This
-- SUBSUMES rungs 1+2 (a single-arg, or any single fixed-position, descent is
-- the k = the-fixed-position special case). It REPAIRS the hole: in the
-- cross-position cases the first non-Eq position is RelUnknown ⇒ NOT
-- lex-decreasing ⇒ `Unknown` (never wrongly `Total`).
-- RUNG 3 (slice B) = THE SIZE-CHANGE GRAPH CLOSURE (Phase 3d) — see the full
-- RUNG 3 (slice B) block below `totScrutDecreasable` for the principle, the LJB
-- citation, and the soundness argument. Slice B replaces slice A's fixed-order
-- lexicographic scan (`totCallLexDec`, RETIRED) with the COMPLETE-for-the-size-
-- change-abstraction criterion: build a size-change graph per self-call site
-- (the slice-A per-position relations `totPosIsEq`/`totPosIsLt` REUSED as the
-- edge oracle, now over ALL source × target pairs), take the fuel-bounded
-- transitive closure under composition, and accept iff every IDEMPOTENT graph in
-- the closure has a strictly-descending self-edge. A strict superset of slice A:
-- it proves PERMUTED / reordering / multi-step-rotation descents that no fixed
-- order exposes (`f a b = if a > 0 then f b (a - 1) else 0` ⇒ Total) while
-- KEEPING the cross-position soundness repairs `Unknown` (their `G = {a →↓ b}`
-- has the empty idempotent `G ; G = {}`, no strict self-edge).
-- RUNG 3 (slice C) = MUTUAL RECURSION (Phase 3e) — the LAST termination class.
-- See the full RUNG 3 (slice C) block below the slice-B section for the principle,
-- the LJB general-form citation, and the soundness argument. Slice C generalizes
-- the per-function size-change closure to a CALL GRAPH over a SET of functions:
-- graphs become `{from, to, edges}` morphisms `caller → callee`; composition is
-- restricted to matching intermediate functions (`G.to == H.from`); the program
-- terminates iff every IDEMPOTENT graph `f → f` in the closure has a
-- strictly-descending self-edge. A strict SUPERSET of slice B (the single
-- function is the one-object special case — `checkStructuralTotality` is now
-- singleton sugar over `checkMutualTotality`, so the 40 slice-B verdicts are
-- preserved by construction). The MUTUAL fence is REMOVED — slice C ships it
-- (the structural `even`/`odd`-shaped mutual win, the measure mutual win, the
-- 3-function cycle all prove `Total`; the canaries `f a = g a` / `g b = f b` and
-- the permutation ping-pong stay `Unknown`). UNBLOCKS the kernel gate.
-- FENCED (inherited): `≠ 0` / `== 0` equality guards (deriving `m > 0` from
-- `m ≠ 0` needs a ℕ TYPE, not a name-set, so `== 0`-guarded mutual `even`/`odd`
-- stays `Unknown`); k ≥ 2 / non-`sub` measures; and SCC DISCOVERY (the group is
-- an explicit input — D-3e-4 — slice C does not find the mutually-recursive set
-- itself). STILL ADVISORY (no kernel-gate wiring this slice — that is the next
-- slice, now unblocked).
--
-- THE THREE-VALUED VERDICT (design/unified-static-analysis.md, D-B):
--   Total            — termination proven (a rung found a decrease, or no recursion)
--   Partial reason   — provably non-total, or declared `@partial`  ⇒ hard-reject
--   Unknown reason   — no rung decided YET                          ⇒ warn (climb), reject on proof-paths
--
-- SOUNDNESS DISCIPLINE (totality must NEVER wrongly say `Total`): variable
-- shadowing is handled — a binder (lambda param, match-arm pattern var) that
-- re-uses a name REMOVES it from the smaller/scrutinizable/positivity sets
-- before the body is walked, so a fresh same-named binding is never mistaken
-- for the structurally-smaller one (or the `> 0` fact) it shadows. THREE sets
-- are threaded, plus the constant `params` (the full parameter list, needed at
-- each self-call site to pair positions): `scrut` (names whose destructuring
-- yields smaller vars — the params plus any smaller var), `origins` (the
-- ORIGIN-TRACKED smaller-var set — a `List {name, origin}` pairing each
-- strictly-smaller variable with the ROOT PARAMETER it is a sub-term of; rung 3
-- needs "smaller than WHICH param", which the rung-1/2 flat `decr` set could
-- NOT answer — so `decr` BECAME `origins`), and `pos` (rung 2 — the facts an
-- enclosing guard proves about named variables: `> 0`, `≤ 2^53`, a non-NaN
-- Number; all three make a `std:sub p 1` arg count as a measure decrease at p's
-- OWN position, 2026-10-03). every `origins` name ∈ `scrut`; params ∈
-- `scrut` but NOT `origins` (a param is not smaller than itself); `pos` is
-- seeded empty and grown only by guards (never by destructuring — a field is
-- structurally smaller, not known `> 0`). The WALK now COLLECTS a `List Graph`
-- (every self-call's size-change graph, with its local pos/origins context) —
-- `totCollectGraphs`, NOT the boolean `totHasBadCall` — and the DECISION is the
-- closure-based SCT criterion (`totSctTerminating`), not the fixed-order lex scan
-- (`totCallLexDec`, RETIRED — subsumed by the closure). The position-agnostic
-- "some arg decreases" fold (the rung-1/2 shortcut) was already RETIRED at slice
-- A — it was unsound for multi-arg.
--
-- INPUT: the irreducible core `Expr` (7 cases, `fenel/std/expr.fenel`) — the
-- surface `if`/`let`/`do` are already lowered (ECall "if" / applied-ELambda /
-- sequence) so this walks 7 cases. Plain ADTs (no `$`-key barrier): the body
-- pattern-matches `ELit`/`EVar`/`ECall`/`ELambda`/`EMatch`/`EConstruct`/
-- `ERecord` and `PatLit`/`PatVar`/`PatWildcard`/`PatConstruct` directly. The
-- idiom (named-field patterns, `head`/`tail`/`appendItem` list folds, arm
-- `{pattern, body}` records) mirrors `desugar.fenel` + `match-structural.fenel`.
--
-- NOTE this checker is itself structurally recursive (decreasing on the Expr
-- subtree / the list tail) — it would pass its own rung-1 check once mutual
-- recursion across the tot* helpers is supported (Phase 2/3).
-- =========================================================================


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Totality — the three-valued verdict ADT.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@entity
@label "Totality"
@description "A totality verdict: Total (termination proven, or no recursion), Partial (provably non-total, or declared @partial — a hard-reject), or Unknown (no rung has decided yet — a warning during the rung climb, a reject on proof-carrying paths). The reason string carries the human-readable justification for Partial / Unknown."
Totality =
  Total
  | Partial reason: String
  | Unknown reason: String


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- totOr — eager boolean disjunction over the finite tree/list walk. (Not
-- short-circuit; every recursion here is on a strictly smaller subtree or
-- list tail, so eager evaluation terminates. Keeps the folds free of
-- `if`-in-`else`-with-`case` shapes.)
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "tot: or"
@description "Eager boolean disjunction used by the totality tree/list folds. Returns True if either operand is True."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
totOr : (x: Bool) -> (y: Bool) -> Bool
totOr x y = if x then True else y


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- totNameElem — membership of a name in a name-list (List String).
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "tot: name elem"
@description "True when `name` occurs in the name-list. List iteration via the head/tail Maybe-returning natives (the engine-body idiom)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
totNameElem : (name: String) -> (list: a) -> Bool
totNameElem name list =
  case head list of
    Nothing -> False
    Just x ->
      case tail list of
        Nothing -> eq x name
        Just rest -> totOr (eq x name) (totNameElem name rest)


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- totRemoveOne / totRemoveAll — drop name(s) from a name-list (shadowing).
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "tot: remove-one tail"
@description "Recurse on the tail of a name-list for totRemoveOne. Internal split (keeps totRemoveOne free of case-in-let)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
totRemoveOneTail : (n: String) -> (list: a) -> a
totRemoveOneTail n list =
  case tail list of
    Nothing -> []
    Just rest -> totRemoveOne n rest

@label "tot: remove-one"
@description "Remove every occurrence of name `n` from the name-list. Used for variable shadowing (a binder re-using a name drops the prior smaller/scrutinizable binding)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
totRemoveOne : (n: String) -> (list: a) -> a
totRemoveOne n list =
  case head list of
    Nothing -> []
    Just x ->
      let restRemoved = totRemoveOneTail n list
      if eq x n then restRemoved else appendItem x restRemoved

@label "tot: remove-all"
@description "Remove every name in `names` from `list`. Applies the shadow-removal of a binder's whole bound-var set to a smaller/scrutinizable set."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
totRemoveAll : (names: a) -> (list: a) -> a
totRemoveAll names list =
  case head names of
    Nothing -> list
    Just n ->
      let list2 = totRemoveOne n list
      case tail names of
        Nothing -> list2
        Just rest -> totRemoveAll rest list2


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- totAppendAll — append every name in `names` to `list`.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "tot: append-all"
@description "Append every name in `names` to `list`. Adds a match-arm's constructor-bound (structurally-smaller) vars to the smaller/scrutinizable sets."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
totAppendAll : (names: a) -> (list: a) -> a
totAppendAll names list =
  case head names of
    Nothing -> list
    Just n ->
      let list2 = appendItem n list
      case tail names of
        Nothing -> list2
        Just rest -> totAppendAll rest list2


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Pattern variable collection — `totCollectAllVars` (every bound var, for
-- shadow removal) and `totCollectCtorVars` (only vars UNDER a PatConstruct,
-- the structurally-smaller ones).
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "tot: collect all pattern vars"
@description "Collect EVERY variable a pattern binds (top-level PatVar + all nested), for shadow removal. PatLit / PatWildcard bind nothing."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
totCollectAllVars : (pattern: Pattern) -> (acc: a) -> a
totCollectAllVars pattern acc =
  case pattern of
    PatVar { name = n } -> appendItem n acc
    PatConstruct { args = subs } -> totCollectAllVarsList subs acc
    _ -> acc

@label "tot: collect all pattern vars (list)"
@description "Fold totCollectAllVars over a list of sub-patterns (a PatConstruct's args)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
totCollectAllVarsList : (subs: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
totCollectAllVarsList subs acc =
  case head subs of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just sp ->
      let acc2 = totCollectAllVars sp acc
      case tail subs of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> totCollectAllVarsList rest acc2

@label "tot: ctor-var step"
@description "One sub-pattern's contribution to the structurally-smaller var set: a PatVar field is smaller; a nested PatConstruct's vars are smaller too; PatLit / PatWildcard contribute nothing."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
totCtorVarStep : (sp: Pattern) -> (acc: a) -> a
totCtorVarStep sp acc =
  case sp of
    PatVar { name = n } -> appendItem n acc
    PatConstruct { args = nested } -> totCollectCtorVarsList nested acc
    _ -> acc

@label "tot: collect ctor vars (list)"
@description "Fold totCtorVarStep over a PatConstruct's sub-patterns — the structurally-smaller variables introduced by destructuring."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
totCollectCtorVarsList : (subs: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
totCollectCtorVarsList subs acc =
  case head subs of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just sp ->
      let acc2 = totCtorVarStep sp acc
      case tail subs of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> totCollectCtorVarsList rest acc2

@label "tot: collect ctor vars"
@description "The structurally-smaller variables a pattern introduces: only the vars UNDER a PatConstruct (fields of a destructured value). A bare top-level PatVar binds a same-size alias, NOT a smaller term, so it contributes nothing."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
totCollectCtorVars : (pattern: Pattern) -> (acc: a) -> a
totCollectCtorVars pattern acc =
  case pattern of
    PatConstruct { args = subs } -> totCollectCtorVarsList subs acc
    _ -> acc


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ORIGIN TRACKING (rung 3, slice A) — the `decr` flat smaller-var set BECAME
-- `origins : List {name, origin}`, pairing each strictly-smaller variable with
-- the ROOT PARAMETER it is a structural sub-term of. The position-aware RelLt
-- needs "smaller than WHICH param", which the flat set could not answer. The
-- origin is ALWAYS a parameter name (the root of the destructuring chain). The
-- entry field is `name` (NOT `var` — `var` is the JSON-Logic variable operator;
-- `name` mirrors the existing `EVar {name}` / `{name, set}` assoc-list shape and
-- side-steps any parse ambiguity).
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "tot: lookup origin"
@description "The origin param of a smaller var `v` in `origins`, or Nothing when `v` is not a tracked smaller var (a parameter, or an unrelated name). Maybe-returning (not a sentinel string) so callers pattern-match. Folds over `origins` comparing entry.name == v."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
totLookupOrigin : (v: String) -> (origins: a) -> Maybe String
totLookupOrigin v origins =
  case head origins of
    Nothing -> Nothing
    Just entry ->
      if eq entry.name v
        then Just entry.origin
        else
          case tail origins of
            Nothing -> Nothing
            Just rest -> totLookupOrigin v rest

@label "tot: origin is param"
@description "True when `v`'s origin is EXACTLY `p` — i.e. `v` is a strict structural sub-term of parameter `p`. Drives RelLt-structural at p's OWN position. Folds over `origins` comparing entry.name == v AND entry.origin == p."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
totOriginIs : (v: String) -> (p: String) -> (origins: a) -> Bool
totOriginIs v p origins =
  case head origins of
    Nothing -> False
    Just entry ->
      let thisMatch = if eq entry.name v then eq entry.origin p else False
      case tail origins of
        Nothing -> thisMatch
        Just rest -> totOr thisMatch (totOriginIs v p rest)

@label "tot: root origin of scrutinee"
@description "The ROOT param of a destructurable scrutinee expression: when `s` is `EVar v`, `v`'s origin if it is itself a smaller var (transitively a param), else `v` (a param is its own root). Non-EVar ⇒ \"\" (unused — only called when canDestr already gated `s ∈ scrut`, so `s` is an EVar). Threads the \"sub-term of WHICH param\" fact through nested destructuring."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
totRootOrigin : (s: Expr) -> (origins: a) -> String
totRootOrigin s origins =
  case s of
    EVar { name = v } ->
      case totLookupOrigin v origins of
        Nothing -> v
        Just o -> o
    _ -> ""

@label "tot: origins remove-one tail"
@description "Recurse on the tail of `origins` for totOriginsRemoveOne. Internal split (keeps totOriginsRemoveOne free of case-in-let)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
totOriginsRemoveOneTail : (n: String) -> (origins: a) -> a
totOriginsRemoveOneTail n origins =
  case tail origins of
    Nothing -> []
    Just rest -> totOriginsRemoveOne n rest

@label "tot: origins remove-one"
@description "Remove every origins entry whose name is `n` (variable shadowing over the origin-tracked set — a binder re-using a name drops the prior smaller binding). Mirrors totRemoveOne but over the {name, origin} records."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
totOriginsRemoveOne : (n: String) -> (origins: a) -> a
totOriginsRemoveOne n origins =
  case head origins of
    Nothing -> []
    Just entry ->
      let restRemoved = totOriginsRemoveOneTail n origins
      if eq entry.name n then restRemoved else appendItem entry restRemoved

@label "tot: origins remove-all"
@description "Remove every entry whose name is in `names` from `origins`. Applies a binder's whole bound-var set's shadow-removal to the origin-tracked smaller set (mirrors totRemoveAll)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
totOriginsRemoveAll : (names: a) -> (origins: a) -> a
totOriginsRemoveAll names origins =
  case head names of
    Nothing -> origins
    Just n ->
      let origins2 = totOriginsRemoveOne n origins
      case tail names of
        Nothing -> origins2
        Just rest -> totOriginsRemoveAll rest origins2

@label "tot: origins add ctor-vars"
@description "Add `{name = ctorVar, origin = root}` for each destructured ctor-var — they all share the scrutinee's root param. Mirrors totAppendAll, attaching the origin (rung 3's per-var root-param tracking)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
totOriginsAddCtor : (ctorVars: a) -> (root: String) -> (origins: a) -> a
totOriginsAddCtor ctorVars root origins =
  case head ctorVars of
    Nothing -> origins
    Just cv ->
      let entry = { name = cv, origin = root }
      let origins2 = appendItem entry origins
      case tail ctorVars of
        Nothing -> origins2
        Just rest -> totOriginsAddCtor rest root origins2


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- THE PER-POSITION RELATIONS + the lexicographic scan (rung 3, slice A). Per
-- position `i` (param `pᵢ`, argument `argᵢ`): RelEq (argᵢ = EVar pᵢ), RelLt
-- (structural `EVar v` with origin pᵢ, OR guarded `sub pᵢ 1` with pᵢ ∈ pos),
-- else RelUnknown. The scan reads left-to-right: the first non-Eq position must
-- be Lt (lex-decreasing) — any other shape there FAILS (cross-position lands in
-- RelUnknown, so the hole is repaired).
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "tot: position RelEq"
@description "True when `arg` is `EVar p` — the position's OWN parameter, unchanged, in its own slot (RelEq). Any other shape ⇒ False."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
totPosIsEq : (p: String) -> (arg: Expr) -> Bool
totPosIsEq p arg =
  case arg of
    EVar { name = v } -> eq v p
    _ -> False

@label "tot: sub is p-minus-one guarded"
@description "True when the `sub` sub-args `s` are exactly `[EVar p, ELit 1]` (the operand is the position's OWN param `p`) AND the branch facts make the decrement strict and well-founded (totCanDecrement). The k=1 fence (inherited rung-2b): only a unit decrement of p itself. Specialized from the retired rung-2 `totSubVarOne` — the var MUST be `p`, not any var in pos."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
totSubIsPMinusOne : (p: String) -> (s: a) -> (pos: a) -> Bool
totSubIsPMinusOne p s pos =
  case head s of
    Nothing -> False
    Just a0 ->
      case tail s of
        Nothing -> False
        Just rest ->
          case head rest of
            Nothing -> False
            Just a1 -> totSubPOne p pos a0 a1

@label "tot: sub operands = (p, 1)"
@description "Helper for totSubIsPMinusOne: True when `a0` is `EVar p` (the position's own param) and `a1` is `ELit 1`, AND the branch facts make `p - 1` a strict, well-founded descent in the runtime number representation (totCanDecrement: p > 0, p ≤ 2^53, p a non-NaN number). Any other shape ⇒ False (sound under-approximation — cross-position `sub q 1` at p's slot, q ≠ p, is RelUnknown here)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
totSubPOne : (p: String) -> (pos: a) -> (a0: Expr) -> (a1: Expr) -> Bool
totSubPOne p pos a0 a1 =
  case a0 of
    EVar { name = v } ->
      case a1 of
        ELit { value = k } ->
          if eq v p
            then (if eq k 1 then totCanDecrement p pos else False)
            else False
        _ -> False
    _ -> False

@label "tot: position RelLt"
@description "True when `arg` is strictly LESS than the position's OWN param `p` (RelLt): structural (`EVar v` with origin(v) = p — a strict sub-term of p in p's slot) OR guarded measure (`std:sub p 1` — the canonical trusted id — under totCanDecrement). A var whose origin is a DIFFERENT param, a construction, or any unrecognized shape ⇒ False (RelUnknown — the cross-position repair)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
totPosIsLt : (p: String) -> (arg: Expr) -> (pos: a) -> (origins: a) -> Bool
totPosIsLt p arg pos origins =
  case arg of
    EVar { name = v } -> totOriginIs v p origins
    ECall { fnId = f, args = s } -> if eq f "std:sub" then totSubIsPMinusOne p s pos else False
    _ -> False

@label "tot: small list tail"
@description "The tail of a list, or [] when empty — a total `tail` for the parallel param/arg scan (decreasing on the list, no indexing)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
totTail : (xs: a) -> a
totTail xs =
  case tail xs of
    Nothing -> []
    Just r -> r

-- (`totCallLexDec` — slice A's fixed-order lexicographic scan — is RETIRED:
-- the size-change graph closure (RUNG 3 slice B, below) proves everything the
-- lex-identity scan did and more, so keeping the dead fixed-order shortcut
-- alongside would only invite regression. Its inputs — `params` / `args` /
-- `pos` / `origins` — now feed the `totCallSiteGraphCross` edge builder. The
-- per-position relations `totPosIsEq` / `totPosIsLt` are REUSED verbatim as the
-- edge oracle: slice A applied them on the DIAGONAL only; slice B applies them
-- to ALL source-param × target-position pairs.)


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- totScrutDecreasable — is a match scrutinee a variable we can destructure
-- into smaller vars? (a parameter, or an already-smaller var ⇒ in `scrut`.)
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "tot: scrutinee destructurable"
@description "True when the match scrutinee is a bare variable in the `scrut` set (a parameter or an already-smaller var), so destructuring it yields structurally-smaller bindings."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
totScrutDecreasable : (scrut: a) -> (s: Expr) -> Bool
totScrutDecreasable scrut s =
  case s of
    EVar { name = v } -> totNameElem v scrut
    _ -> False


-- =========================================================================
-- RUNG 2 — the guard recognizer (`totPosFromCond` / `totPosFromCondNeg`).
--
-- The narrowing that backs rung-2's soundness obligation, RE-EXPRESSED over
-- the core `Expr` + a `pos` NAME-set (NOT a call into `narrowFromCondition`:
-- that operates on ExprMarker + a SetMarker env — a DIFFERENT representation;
-- the inputs are genuinely different ADTs, so this is narrowing specialized to
-- the `v > 0` predicate, not duplicated decision logic — D-3a-3). `pos` is the
-- list of branch facts ({name, fact} records: "lower" v > 0, "upper" v ≤ 2^53,
-- "number" v a non-NaN Number — see totFactsFromCompare) known in the current
-- branch (a set of names known `> 0` until 2026-10-03).
--
-- `totPosFromCond cond pos` extends `pos` with every var the condition PROVES
-- `> 0` in the TRUE branch; `totPosFromCondNeg cond pos` does the same for the
-- FALSE (else) branch (the negation). The and/or asymmetry is mirrored EXACTLY:
-- the true-branch can narrow an `and` (every conjunct holds) but NOT an `or`;
-- the false-branch can narrow an `or` (every disjunct is false) but NOT an
-- `and`. Any shape not recognized adds NOTHING (sound under-approximation — a
-- wrong `> 0` is the unsoundness this rung exists to refuse).
--
-- TRUSTED IDENTITIES ONLY (2026-10-03). A fact is read off a comparison,
-- a conjunction/disjunction or a subtraction only when its head is the
-- CANONICAL id of the std primitive (`std:gt`, `std:gte`, `std:lt`, `std:lte`,
-- `std:and`, `std:or`, `std:sub` — totIsTrustedPrimitive), never off the
-- spelling: a user function named `gt` or `sub` means whatever its body says,
-- and before this repair `gt a b = True; sub a b = a; loop n = if gt n 0 then
-- loop (sub n 1) else 0` read Total. Stored bodies keep source spellings (the
-- desugar codenames `gt` / `sub` … of fixity-resolve.fenel), so each caller
-- resolves them first: the kernel projection rewrites a head whose spelling
-- denotes exactly one registry id, that id being a trusted primitive
-- (analyze.fenel anaCanonicalizeTrusted), and inference rewrites a head its
-- exact routing row resolves to one (inferenceTotalityCallHead). A head that is
-- ambiguous, unresolved or user-defined stays a spelling and yields no fact.
-- =========================================================================

@label "tot: trusted primitive id"
@description "True when `id` is the canonical registry id of a std primitive whose meaning the size-change oracle relies on: the comparisons std:gt / std:gte / std:lt / std:lte, the connectives std:and / std:or, and the decrement std:sub. Only heads already resolved to one of these ids yield a positivity, bound or descent fact; a bare spelling never does (a user function may share the name)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totIsTrustedPrimitive : (id: String) -> Bool
totIsTrustedPrimitive id = elem id ["std:sub", "std:gt", "std:gte", "std:lt", "std:lte", "std:and", "std:or"]

@label "tot: add a branch fact"
@description "Record that the branch proves fact `kind` about variable `v`: \"lower\" (v > 0), \"upper\" (v ≤ 2^53, where subtracting 1 from a JS Number is exact) or \"number\" (v is a Number and not NaN — only a comparison that evaluated to TRUE proves it: std:gt and friends answer false for NaN and for mixed operand types). Facts are records {name, fact} in the `pos` list."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totAddFact : (v: String) -> (kind: String) -> (pos: a) -> a
totAddFact v kind pos =
  let entry = { name = v, fact = kind }
  appendItem entry pos

@label "tot: has a branch fact"
@description "True when the branch facts `pos` hold fact `kind` (\"lower\" / \"upper\" / \"number\") about variable `v`."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totHasFact : (v: String) -> (kind: String) -> (pos: a) -> Bool
totHasFact v kind pos =
  fold (\found x -> if found then True else if eq x.name v then eq x.fact kind else False) False pos

@label "tot: forget facts about shadowed names"
@description "Drop every branch fact about a name in `names` (a binder that re-uses the name hides the variable the fact was about)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totFactsForget : (names: a) -> (pos: b) -> b
totFactsForget names pos = filter (\x -> not (elem x.name names)) pos

@label "tot: unit decrement is a strict well-founded descent"
@description "True when `p - 1` strictly decreases `p` in a well-founded order AS JS NUMBERS COMPUTE IT: p > 0 (\"lower\"), p ≤ 2^53 (\"upper\": below it subtracting 1 is exact, above it `1e20 - 1 = 1e20` and `Infinity - 1 = Infinity`), and p a non-NaN Number (\"number\": a NaN or a non-number satisfies every NEGATED comparison, so `if n <= 0 then 0 else f (n - 1)` loops on NaN). Under all three, ⌈p⌉ is a natural number that drops by one per call. 2026-10-03: before, `p > 0` alone (or the else branch of `p <= 0`) was accepted."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totCanDecrement : (p: String) -> (pos: a) -> Bool
totCanDecrement p pos =
  and (totHasFact p "lower" pos) (and (totHasFact p "upper" pos) (totHasFact p "number" pos))

@label "tot: flip a comparison"
@description "The relation read from the other side: `k > v` is `v < k`. gt ↔ lt, gte ↔ lte."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totRelFlip : (rel: String) -> String
totRelFlip rel =
  if eq rel "gt" then "lt" else if eq rel "lt" then "gt" else if eq rel "gte" then "lte" else if eq rel "lte" then "gte" else ""

@label "tot: relation holding in a branch"
@description "The relation `v rel k` holding in the TRUE branch (`truth`), or its negation in the FALSE branch: not (v > k) is v ≤ k, and so on. The negation is exact only for non-NaN numbers, which is why a false-branch relation never contributes the \"number\" fact."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totRelUnder : (rel: String) -> (truth: Bool) -> String
totRelUnder rel truth =
  if truth then rel
  else if eq rel "gt" then "lte" else if eq rel "gte" then "lt" else if eq rel "lt" then "gte" else if eq rel "lte" then "gt" else ""

@label "tot: facts from a variable-literal relation"
@description "Extend the branch facts with what `v rel k` proves for a NUMERIC literal k (a non-number literal proves nothing): v > k with k ≥ 0, or v ≥ k with k > 0, gives \"lower\"; v < k or v ≤ k with k ≤ 2^53 gives \"upper\"; and when the comparison itself evaluated to TRUE (`direct`), \"number\"."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totFactsFromRel : (v: String) -> (rel: String) -> (k: b) -> (direct: Bool) -> (pos: a) -> a
totFactsFromRel v rel k direct pos =
  if not (isNumber k) then pos
  else
    let withNumber = if direct then totAddFact v "number" pos else pos
    let lower = if eq rel "gt" then gte k 0 else if eq rel "gte" then gt k 0 else False
    let upper = if eq rel "lt" then lte k 9007199254740992 else if eq rel "lte" then lte k 9007199254740992 else False
    let withLower = if lower then totAddFact v "lower" withNumber else withNumber
    if upper then totAddFact v "upper" withLower else withLower

@label "tot: facts from a comparison"
@description "The facts a trusted comparison `f a0 a1` (std:gt / std:gte / std:lt / std:lte only — totIsTrustedPrimitive) proves about a variable compared with a literal, in its TRUE branch (`truth`) or its FALSE branch. Either orientation (`v > 0`, `0 < v`); any other shape or head proves nothing."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totFactsFromCompare : (f: String) -> (a0: Expr) -> (a1: Expr) -> (truth: Bool) -> (pos: a) -> a
totFactsFromCompare f a0 a1 truth pos =
  let rel = if eq f "std:gt" then "gt" else if eq f "std:gte" then "gte" else if eq f "std:lt" then "lt" else if eq f "std:lte" then "lte" else ""
  if eq rel "" then pos
  else
    case a0 of
      EVar { name = v } ->
        case a1 of
          ELit { value = k } -> totFactsFromRel v (totRelUnder rel truth) k truth pos
          _ -> pos
      ELit { value = k } ->
        case a1 of
          EVar { name = v } -> totFactsFromRel v (totRelUnder (totRelFlip rel) truth) k truth pos
          _ -> pos
      _ -> pos

@label "tot: positivity from comparison (true-branch)"
@description "The facts a binary comparison proves in its TRUE branch, given its fnId and two operands (totFactsFromCompare with truth = True): positivity, the exact-decrement bound and Number-ness of the compared variable. Unrecognized fnId or shape ⇒ pos unchanged."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3a"
@category "engine-internal"
totPosFromCompare : (f: String) -> (a0: Expr) -> (a1: Expr) -> (pos: a) -> a
totPosFromCompare f a0 a1 pos = totFactsFromCompare f a0 a1 True pos

@label "tot: positivity from comparison (false-branch)"
@description "The facts the negated comparison proves (what the FALSE/else branch knows; totFactsFromCompare with truth = False): positivity or the exact-decrement bound of the compared variable, never its Number-ness (NaN and non-numbers fail every comparison). Unrecognized fnId or shape ⇒ pos unchanged."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3a"
@category "engine-internal"
totPosFromCompareNeg : (f: String) -> (a0: Expr) -> (a1: Expr) -> (pos: a) -> a
totPosFromCompareNeg f a0 a1 pos = totFactsFromCompare f a0 a1 False pos

@label "tot: binary operands → positivity (true)"
@description "Extract the two operands of a binary comparison `ECall f args` and apply totPosFromCompare. Fewer than two operands ⇒ pos unchanged."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3a"
@category "engine-internal"
totPosFromBinary : (f: String) -> (args: a) -> (pos: b) -> b
totPosFromBinary f args pos =
  case head args of
    Nothing -> pos
    Just a0 ->
      case tail args of
        Nothing -> pos
        Just rest ->
          case head rest of
            Nothing -> pos
            Just a1 -> totPosFromCompare f a0 a1 pos

@label "tot: binary operands → positivity (false)"
@description "Extract the two operands of a binary comparison `ECall f args` and apply totPosFromCompareNeg (the else-branch positivity). Fewer than two operands ⇒ pos unchanged."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3a"
@category "engine-internal"
totPosFromBinaryNeg : (f: String) -> (args: a) -> (pos: b) -> b
totPosFromBinaryNeg f args pos =
  case head args of
    Nothing -> pos
    Just a0 ->
      case tail args of
        Nothing -> pos
        Just rest ->
          case head rest of
            Nothing -> pos
            Just a1 -> totPosFromCompareNeg f a0 a1 pos

@label "tot: fold positivity over and-conjuncts"
@description "Fold totPosFromCond over the conjuncts of an `and` (true-branch): every conjunct holds, so each narrowing applies in sequence."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3a"
@category "engine-internal"
totPosFoldAnd : (args: a) -> (pos: b) -> b
totPosFoldAnd args pos =
  case head args of
    Nothing -> pos
    Just c ->
      let pos2 = totPosFromCond c pos
      case tail args of
        Nothing -> pos2
        Just rest -> totPosFoldAnd rest pos2

@label "tot: fold neg-positivity over or-disjuncts"
@description "Fold totPosFromCondNeg over the disjuncts of an `or` (false-branch): the else branch of `if (or [..])` holds only when EVERY disjunct is false, so each negated narrowing applies in sequence."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3a"
@category "engine-internal"
totPosFoldOrNeg : (args: a) -> (pos: b) -> b
totPosFoldOrNeg args pos =
  case head args of
    Nothing -> pos
    Just c ->
      let pos2 = totPosFromCondNeg c pos
      case tail args of
        Nothing -> pos2
        Just rest -> totPosFoldOrNeg rest pos2

@label "tot: positivity from guard (true-branch)"
@description "Extend `pos` with every variable the condition PROVES `> 0` in its TRUE branch. Handles `and` (fold over conjuncts) and the four binary comparisons; the true-branch CANNOT narrow an `or` (the and/or asymmetry), so an `or` and any unrecognized shape leave `pos` unchanged (sound under-approximation)."
@tags "engine" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3a"
totPosFromCond : (cond: Expr) -> (pos: a) -> a
totPosFromCond cond pos =
  case cond of
    ECall { fnId = f, args = args } ->
      if eq f "std:and" then totPosFoldAnd args pos
      else totPosFromBinary f args pos
    _ -> pos

@label "tot: positivity from guard (false-branch)"
@description "Extend `pos` with every variable the condition's NEGATION proves `> 0` (the else branch). Handles `or` (fold the negated narrowing over disjuncts) and the four negated binary comparisons; the false-branch CANNOT narrow an `and` (the and/or asymmetry), so an `and` and any unrecognized shape leave `pos` unchanged (sound under-approximation)."
@tags "engine" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3a"
totPosFromCondNeg : (cond: Expr) -> (pos: a) -> a
totPosFromCondNeg cond pos =
  case cond of
    ECall { fnId = f, args = args } ->
      if eq f "std:or" then totPosFoldOrNeg args pos
      else totPosFromBinaryNeg f args pos
    _ -> pos


-- =========================================================================
-- RUNG 3 (slice B) — THE SIZE-CHANGE GRAPH CLOSURE (Lee–Jones–Ben-Amram, "The
-- Size-Change Principle for Program Termination", POPL 2001). The complete
-- (for the size-change abstraction) single-function termination criterion;
-- subsumes rungs 1+2+3a and proves PERMUTED / reordering descents for which NO
-- fixed parameter order works (`f a b = if a > 0 then f b (a - 1) else 0` —
-- terminating, but slice A fences it `Unknown` because position 0 gets `b`).
--
-- THE SIZE-CHANGE GRAPH of a self-call `f(arg₀ … argₙ₋₁)` (caller params
-- `p₀ … pₙ₋₁`) is a `List Edge`; an edge `{ src, tgt, strict }` records a size
-- relation from a SOURCE param to a callee TARGET param-slot. For every source
-- `pⱼ` and target position `i` (arg `argᵢ` binds the callee's `pᵢ`):
--   • strict edge `pⱼ →↓ pᵢ`  (`strict = true`)  ⟺ `totPosIsLt pⱼ argᵢ pos
--     origins` (argᵢ is a structural sub-term of pⱼ, OR argᵢ = sub pⱼ 1 with
--     pⱼ ∈ pos — the callee's pᵢ is STRICTLY less than the caller's pⱼ);
--   • non-strict edge `pⱼ →↓= pᵢ` (`strict = false`) ⟺ `totPosIsEq pⱼ argᵢ`
--     (argᵢ = EVar pⱼ — the callee's pᵢ is EQUAL/≤ the caller's pⱼ);
--   • no edge otherwise (a construction, an unrelated var, any unrecognized
--     shape). At most one edge per (src, tgt) slot — RelLt and RelEq are
--     mutually exclusive. The per-position relations `totPosIsEq`/`totPosIsLt`
--     are slice A's, REUSED verbatim — slice A read them on the DIAGONAL only;
--     slice B reads them over ALL source × target pairs (the generalization).
--
-- COMPOSITION `G ; H` (G then H, both over the same param set): an edge
-- `x →ʳ z` exists iff some intermediate `y` has `x →ʳ¹ y ∈ G` and `y →ʳ² z ∈ H`;
-- the label is STRICT if r1 OR r2 is strict, else non-strict (`totOr` on the
-- flags). When several intermediates yield `x → z`, the STRONGEST wins
-- (`totAddStrongEdge` — strict dominates). Composition models the size relation
-- after two consecutive calls.
--
-- CLOSURE `S*`. Start with S₀ = the call-site graphs (one per self-call,
-- deduped). Iterate `S_{k+1} = S_k ∪ { normalize(G ; H) : G, H ∈ S_k }` until
-- `S_{k+1} = S_k`. The set of distinct graphs over n params is finite (each of
-- n² slots ∈ {none, ↓=, ↓} ⇒ ≤ 3^(n²) graphs), so the closure TERMINATES — the
-- fuel is the structural-decreasing measure (`totClose`, seeded 256, early-exit
-- on no-change) AND a pathological backstop; fuel exhaustion ⇒ `Unknown` (a
-- SOUND under-approximation — we NEVER check a PARTIAL closure for `Total`).
--
-- THE SCT CRITERION. The recursion is size-change terminating iff EVERY
-- IDEMPOTENT graph `G` in the closure (`G ; G = G`) has a strictly-descending
-- SELF-edge (∃x. x →↓ x ∈ G). An idempotent graph describes a "stable" infinite
-- call path; if every such path strictly decreases SOME parameter forever, no
-- infinite computation exists (well-foundedness — structural sizes ∈ ℕ, guarded
-- measures ≥ 0 within descent — forbids it).
--
-- WHY SOUND (never a wrong `Total`). Every edge asserts a relation the sound
-- per-position oracle already proved (slice A's soundness, unchanged);
-- composition only DERIVES relations that hold along two-call paths; the SCT
-- theorem is sound. A MISSING edge (under-approximation) only makes the
-- criterion HARDER to satisfy ⇒ `Unknown`, never a wrong `Total`.
-- WHY REPAIR-PRESERVING (the slice-A holes stay `Unknown`). `f a b = case a of
-- Cons h t -> f (Cons h t) t`: arg₀ = Cons h t (construction ⇒ no edge), arg₁ =
-- t (origin a ⇒ strict a →↓ b). G = {a →↓ b}; G ; G = {} (G's only edge target
-- b ≠ its source a, no composition) — the EMPTY idempotent has no strict
-- self-edge ⇒ `Unknown` (✓ `a` never shrinks). Same for the measure
-- cross-position `f (b+1) (a-1)` (same G = {a →↓ b}).
-- WHY SUBSUMES slice A. A lex-identity descent is a special case of SCT (LJB
-- theorem) — every slice-A `Total` keeps its diagonal strict edge into a
-- strict-self-edge idempotent.
-- WHY WINS. Permuted `f a b = if a>0 then f b (a-1) else 0`: arg₀ = b (RelEq vs
-- b ⇒ b →↓= a), arg₁ = a-1 (a ∈ pos ⇒ a →↓ b). G = {b →↓= a, a →↓ b}; G ; G =
-- {a →↓ a, b →↓ b} (idempotent, strict self-edges) ⇒ `Total` (slice A said
-- `Unknown`).
-- SLICE C (rung-3c, Phase 3e) LIFTED this: the bare `List Edge` graph became a
-- `{from, to, edges}` morphism, the walk threads `group` + `fromId` + `fromParams`
-- (not one `selfId`), and composition is guarded by `G.to == H.from` — so MUTUAL
-- recursion (a SET of functions, inter-function edges between DIFFERENT param
-- sets) is now decided. This slice-B section's machinery (the edge ops, the edge
-- composition fold, the closure shape) is REUSED verbatim by slice C below.
-- Inherited fences (slice A): the size-change abstraction tracks only ≤ / < from
-- the name-set oracle, so `≠ 0`/ℕ-typed guards still need a TYPE (`== 0`-guarded
-- Ackermann/even-odd stays `Unknown`), and the k=1 / non-`sub` measure fence is
-- unchanged. STILL ADVISORY (no kernel-gate wiring — slice C's successor).
-- =========================================================================


-- =========================================================================
-- RUNG 3 (slice C) — MUTUAL RECURSION: THE CALL-GRAPH SIZE-CHANGE CLOSURE
-- (Lee–Jones–Ben-Amram general form). The LAST termination class; UNBLOCKS the
-- kernel gate. Generalizes slice B's per-function self-composition to a CALL
-- GRAPH over a SET of functions `{f₀, f₁, …}`, each with its own param list.
--
-- THE CALL GRAPH. A call site `fₐ(…) → fᵦ(arg₀ … argₘ₋₁)` (the call is in fₐ's
-- body; fᵦ's params are q₀ … qₘ₋₁) yields a size-change graph `G : fₐ → fᵦ` — a
-- record `{from = fₐ, to = fᵦ, edges}`. Edges run from the CALLER's params
-- (source) to the CALLEE's param-slots (target), via the SAME per-position oracle
-- slice A/B use (totPosIsLt / totPosIsEq, REUSED verbatim) — only the source set
-- (caller) and target set (callee) now DIFFER (slice B had them equal). The walk
-- totCallSiteGraphGo already separates source `allParams` from target `tgtParams`,
-- so the cross-function build is the SAME walk seeded with caller ≠ callee params.
--
-- COMPOSITION `G ; H` (category structure, PARTIAL). Defined ONLY when
-- `G.to == H.from` (the intermediate function matches): `G : fₐ → fᵦ` and
-- `H : fᵦ → f𝚌` compose to `G ; H : fₐ → f𝚌` (from = G.from, to = H.to, edges =
-- the SAME meet-at-intermediate edge composition slice B uses). When G.to ≠ H.from
-- there is NO composed graph (the pair is SKIPPED — NOT an empty graph, which
-- would pollute the closure with a spurious idempotent). Name collisions across
-- functions are harmless — composition only matches G.edge.tgt to H.edge.src when
-- G.to == H.from, so both names live in the SAME intermediate's param namespace.
--
-- CLOSURE `S*`. S₀ = every call-site graph from EVERY group member's body
-- (totCollectAllMembers, deduped). Iterate S_{k+1} = S_k ∪ { normalize(G ; H) :
-- G,H ∈ S_k, G.to == H.from } until fixpoint. The distinct-graph set is finite
-- (≤ 3^(|from|×|to|) edge-sets per ordered (from,to) pair, finitely many pairs),
-- so the closure TERMINATES — fuel-bounded (256), exhaustion ⇒ `Unknown`.
--
-- THE SCT CRITERION (LJB, general). Size-change terminating iff every IDEMPOTENT
-- graph `G` in the closure (`G.from == G.to` AND `G ; G = G`) has a
-- strictly-descending SELF-edge (∃x. x →↓ x ∈ G.edges). Idempotent graphs are
-- necessarily `f → f` cycles. Intuition: an idempotent `f → f` graph is a stable
-- infinite call path returning to `f`; if every such cycle strictly decreases
-- SOME parameter forever, no infinite computation exists (well-foundedness of the
-- per-parameter domains forbids it).
--
-- WHY SOUND (never a wrong `Total`). Every edge asserts a relation the sound
-- per-position oracle proved (slice A's soundness, unchanged); composition only
-- derives relations holding along multi-call call-graph paths; the LJB theorem is
-- sound for the general multi-function case. A MISSING edge (a call outside the
-- group, an unrecognized shape, fuel exhaustion) only weakens the criterion ⇒
-- `Unknown`, never a wrong `Total`. A partial closure is NEVER checked for `Total`.
-- WHY SUBSUMES slice B. The single function is the one-object special case: every
-- graph is `f → f`, the `from == to` guard is always true, composition is always
-- defined ⇒ the closure + criterion reduce EXACTLY to slice B's.
-- checkStructuralTotality is now SUGAR for checkMutualTotality of a singleton
-- group — the 40 slice-B test verdicts are preserved BY CONSTRUCTION.
-- WHY WINS. Structural mutual `f x = case x of Cons h t -> g t` / `g y = case y
-- of Cons h t -> f t`: G1 = f→g {x →↓ y}, G2 = g→f {y →↓ x}; G1;G2 = f→f {x →↓ x},
-- G2;G1 = g→g {y →↓ y}, both idempotent with a strict self-edge ⇒ `Total`. The
-- measure mutual `f a = if a>0 then g (a-1)` / `g b = if b>0 then f (b-1)` ⇒
-- `Total` likewise. A 3-function cycle `f → g → h → f` surfaces its `f → f`
-- idempotent only after composing THREE graphs — the closure fixpoint catches it.
-- WHY STAYS SOUND on the canaries (MUST be `Unknown`). Mutual non-termination
-- `f a = g a` / `g b = f b`: G1 = f→g {a →↓= b}, G2 = g→f {b →↓= a}; G1;G2 = f→f
-- {a →↓= a} — idempotent with NO strict self-edge ⇒ `Unknown` (f 5 → g 5 → f 5 …
-- diverges). Permutation ping-pong `f a b = g b a` / `g x y = f y x` — the f→f
-- cycle is {a →↓= a, b →↓= b}, no strict self-edge ⇒ `Unknown`.
-- FENCED (inherited): `≠ 0` / `== 0` equality guards need a ℕ TYPE (`== 0`-guarded
-- mutual `even`/`odd` stays `Unknown`); k ≥ 2 / non-`sub` measures; and SCC
-- DISCOVERY — the group is an explicit input (D-3e-4); slice C does not find the
-- mutually-recursive set itself (the gate wiring or a follow-up owns it). STILL
-- ADVISORY (no kernel-gate wiring — the NEXT slice, now unblocked).
-- =========================================================================


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A. The size-change graph representation. A graph is a `List Edge`; an edge is
-- the anonymous record `{ src, tgt, strict }` (src/tgt param-name Strings; the
-- `strict` Bool field VALUE uses lowercase true/false per the solve.fenel idiom
-- — no bare True/False in arg position). A graph SET (the closure) is a
-- `List Graph` = `List (List Edge)`. 0 entity decls (plain List-of-records, the
-- propagate.fenel/totality.fenel plain-record discipline). The canonical graph
-- form has at most one edge per (src, tgt) slot, strict dominating.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "tot: and"
@description "Eager boolean conjunction used by the size-change set/closure folds. Returns y when x is True, else False."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totAnd : (x: Bool) -> (y: Bool) -> Bool
totAnd x y = if x then y else False

@label "tot: bool eq"
@description "Boolean equality (the `strict` flag comparison for edge equality). True when both flags agree. Avoids relying on the scalar `eq` native over JS booleans."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totBoolEq : (x: Bool) -> (y: Bool) -> Bool
totBoolEq x y = if x then y else not y

@label "tot: edge same slot"
@description "True when two edges occupy the SAME (src, tgt) slot — same source param AND same target param — regardless of strictness. Used for canonical-form merge + strict-dominance."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totEdgeSameSlot : (e1: a) -> (e2: a) -> Bool
totEdgeSameSlot e1 e2 = if eq e1.src e2.src then eq e1.tgt e2.tgt else False

@label "tot: edge eq"
@description "Full edge equality: same (src, tgt) slot AND same strict flag. Needed for set-equality of graphs (idempotency + closure dedup)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totEdgeEq : (e1: a) -> (e2: a) -> Bool
totEdgeEq e1 e2 = if totEdgeSameSlot e1 e2 then totBoolEq e1.strict e2.strict else False

@label "tot: edge member"
@description "True when edge `e` (exact src/tgt/strict) occurs in graph `g`. Fold totEdgeEq over g."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totEdgeMember : (e: a) -> (g: b) -> Bool
totEdgeMember e g =
  case head g of
    Nothing -> False
    Just e2 ->
      if totEdgeEq e e2 then True
      else
        case tail g of
          Nothing -> False
          Just rest -> totEdgeMember e rest

@label "tot: edges subset"
@description "True when every edge of edge-list `g` occurs (exactly) in edge-list `h`. The order-independent half of edge-set-equality. (Slice C rename: was totGraphSubset — graphs are now {from,to,edges} records, so the set ops over the EDGE lists are named tot Edges* and the graph-level eq compares from/to too.)"
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
totEdgesSubset : (g: a) -> (h: b) -> Bool
totEdgesSubset g h =
  case head g of
    Nothing -> True
    Just e ->
      let thisIn = totEdgeMember e h
      case tail g of
        Nothing -> thisIn
        Just rest -> totAnd thisIn (totEdgesSubset rest h)

@label "tot: edges eq"
@description "Set-equality of two edge-lists (order-independent): mutual edge-subset. Both are kept in canonical form (one edge per slot, strict-dominant), so set-equality is the right notion for idempotency + closure dedup. (Slice C rename: was totGraphEq, edge-level.)"
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
totEdgesEq : (g: a) -> (h: b) -> Bool
totEdgesEq g h = totAnd (totEdgesSubset g h) (totEdgesSubset h g)

@label "tot: graph eq"
@description "Set-equality of two GRAPHS (slice C): same `from` function, same `to` function, AND set-equal edge lists. A graph is a {from, to, edges} morphism caller→callee; two graphs are equal only when they label the SAME function pair and carry the same canonical edge set. Drives idempotency + closure dedup over the call graph."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totGraphEq : (g: a) -> (h: b) -> Bool
totGraphEq g h = totAnd (eq g.from h.from) (totAnd (eq g.to h.to) (totEdgesEq g.edges h.edges))

@label "tot: graph member"
@description "True when graph `g` (by graph set-equality — from/to/edges) occurs in the graph-set `set`. Fold totGraphEq over set."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totGraphMember : (g: a) -> (set: b) -> Bool
totGraphMember g set =
  case head set of
    Nothing -> False
    Just g2 ->
      if totGraphEq g g2 then True
      else
        case tail set of
          Nothing -> False
          Just rest -> totGraphMember g rest

@label "tot: graph-set subset"
@description "True when every graph of set `s1` occurs (by set-equality) in set `s2`. Half of the closure fixpoint stop-test."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totGraphSetSubset : (s1: a) -> (s2: b) -> Bool
totGraphSetSubset s1 s2 =
  case head s1 of
    Nothing -> True
    Just g ->
      let thisIn = totGraphMember g s2
      case tail s1 of
        Nothing -> thisIn
        Just rest -> totAnd thisIn (totGraphSetSubset rest s2)

@label "tot: graph-set eq"
@description "Set-equality of two graph-sets (mutual graph-subset) — the closure fixpoint stop-test (the round added no new graph)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totGraphSetEq : (s1: a) -> (s2: b) -> Bool
totGraphSetEq s1 s2 = totAnd (totGraphSetSubset s1 s2) (totGraphSetSubset s2 s1)

@label "tot: keep merged edge"
@description "The strict-dominance merge step: build a single edge in `x`'s slot with strict = (x OR e strict), prepended onto the already-rebuilt rest. Helper for totMergeEdge (keeps it free of inline-record-in-then)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totMergeEdgeKeep : (x: a) -> (e: a) -> (rest: b) -> b
totMergeEdgeKeep x e rest =
  let merged = { src = x.src, tgt = x.tgt, strict = totOr x.strict e.strict }
  appendItem merged rest

@label "tot: merge-edge tail"
@description "Recurse on the tail of graph `g` for totMergeEdge (keeps it free of case-in-let)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totMergeEdgeTail : (e: a) -> (g: b) -> b
totMergeEdgeTail e g =
  case tail g of
    Nothing -> []
    Just rest -> totMergeEdge e rest

@label "tot: merge edge (strict-dominant)"
@description "Rebuild graph `g`, OR-ing `e`'s strict flag into the existing edge in the SAME (src, tgt) slot (canonical-form strict-dominance). Non-matching edges pass through. Used only when a slot is already present (else totAddStrongEdge appends)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totMergeEdge : (e: a) -> (g: b) -> b
totMergeEdge e g =
  case head g of
    Nothing -> []
    Just x ->
      let rest2 = totMergeEdgeTail e g
      if totEdgeSameSlot e x then totMergeEdgeKeep x e rest2 else appendItem x rest2

@label "tot: slot present"
@description "True when graph `g` already has an edge in `e`'s (src, tgt) slot. Decides whether totAddStrongEdge merges (strict-dominance) or appends."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totSlotPresent : (e: a) -> (g: b) -> Bool
totSlotPresent e g =
  case head g of
    Nothing -> False
    Just x ->
      if totEdgeSameSlot e x then True
      else
        case tail g of
          Nothing -> False
          Just rest -> totSlotPresent e rest

@label "tot: add strong edge"
@description "Insert edge `e` into graph `g` preserving canonical form: if an edge with the same (src, tgt) slot already exists, OR the strict flags (strict wins); else append. The graph builder AND composition both route through this."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totAddStrongEdge : (e: a) -> (g: b) -> b
totAddStrongEdge e g =
  if totSlotPresent e g then totMergeEdge e g else appendItem e g


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- B. The per-call-site graph builder. Reuse the slice-A per-position relations
-- (`totPosIsLt` / `totPosIsEq`) as the edge oracle, now over ALL source-param ×
-- target-position pairs (slice A read them on the diagonal only). For each
-- target arg, fold over the FULL source param list; for each source, a strict /
-- non-strict / no edge per the oracle.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "tot: strict edge"
@description "Append a strict edge {src, tgt, strict = true} onto the accumulator (the source param strictly dominates the target slot)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totStrictEdge : (src: String) -> (tgt: String) -> (acc: a) -> a
totStrictEdge src tgt acc =
  let e = { src = src, tgt = tgt, strict = true }
  appendItem e acc

@label "tot: non-strict edge"
@description "Append a non-strict edge {src, tgt, strict = false} onto the accumulator (the source param is equal-to/≤ the target slot)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totNonStrictEdge : (src: String) -> (tgt: String) -> (acc: a) -> a
totNonStrictEdge src tgt acc =
  let e = { src = src, tgt = tgt, strict = false }
  appendItem e acc

@label "tot: edge for one source param"
@description "One source param `src`'s contribution to the edges INTO target slot `tgt` (arg `arg`): a strict edge when totPosIsLt (arg ≺ src — structural sub-term or guarded `sub src 1`), a non-strict edge when totPosIsEq (arg = EVar src), else nothing. At most one edge per source."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totEdgeForSrc : (src: String) -> (tgt: String) -> (arg: Expr) -> (pos: a) -> (origins: a) -> (acc: b) -> b
totEdgeForSrc src tgt arg pos origins acc =
  if totPosIsLt src arg pos origins then totStrictEdge src tgt acc
  else if totPosIsEq src arg then totNonStrictEdge src tgt acc
  else acc

@label "tot: edges for one target arg (tail)"
@description "Recurse on the tail of the source-param list for totEdgesForArg (keeps it free of case-in-let)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totEdgesForArgTail : (srcParams: a) -> (tgt: String) -> (arg: Expr) -> (pos: b) -> (origins: c) -> d
totEdgesForArgTail srcParams tgt arg pos origins =
  case tail srcParams of
    Nothing -> []
    Just rest -> totEdgesForArg rest tgt arg pos origins

@label "tot: edges for one target arg"
@description "Fold over the FULL source param list, accumulating each source's edge (strict / non-strict / none) into target slot `tgt` for argument `arg`. Returns the edges into this one slot."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totEdgesForArg : (srcParams: a) -> (tgt: String) -> (arg: Expr) -> (pos: b) -> (origins: c) -> d
totEdgesForArg srcParams tgt arg pos origins =
  case head srcParams of
    Nothing -> []
    Just src ->
      let rest = totEdgesForArgTail srcParams tgt arg pos origins
      totEdgeForSrc src tgt arg pos origins rest

@label "tot: merge edges into a graph"
@description "Fold totAddStrongEdge over a list of edges into the running graph (canonical-form insert, strict-dominant). Used to accumulate one target slot's edges into the call-site graph."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totMergeEdges : (edges: a) -> (acc: b) -> b
totMergeEdges edges acc =
  case head edges of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just e ->
      let acc2 = totAddStrongEdge e acc
      case tail edges of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> totMergeEdges rest acc2

@label "tot: call-site graph walk"
@description "The parallel walk of target params / arguments (decreasing on the tails via totTail, no indexing): for each (tgtName, arg), accumulate totEdgesForArg over the FULL source param list into the running graph. Ran out of either list ⇒ the accumulated graph (an arity mismatch yields fewer edges — sound: a missing edge only weakens the criterion)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totCallSiteGraphGo : (allParams: a) -> (tgtParams: b) -> (args: c) -> (pos: d) -> (origins: e) -> (acc: f) -> f
totCallSiteGraphGo allParams tgtParams args pos origins acc =
  case head tgtParams of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just tgtName ->
      case head args of
        Nothing -> acc
        Just arg ->
          let edges = totEdgesForArg allParams tgtName arg pos origins
          let acc2 = totMergeEdges edges acc
          totCallSiteGraphGo allParams (totTail tgtParams) (totTail args) pos origins acc2

@label "tot: cross-function call-site graph"
@description "The size-change graph `G : fromId → toId` of ONE call site `toId(args)` in `fromId`'s body (slice C, generalizing slice B's single-function totCallSiteGraph): seeds the parallel param/arg walk with SOURCE = the caller's param list (callerParams) and TARGET = the callee's param list (calleeParams) — DIFFERENT sets for a mutual call, EQUAL for a self-call — then wraps the edge list in a {from, to, edges} morphism record. totCallSiteGraphGo is REUSED verbatim (it already separates source `allParams` from target `tgtParams`). The edges are built via a `let` then the literal (the inline-record-in-arg surprise)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totCallSiteGraphCross : (fromId: String) -> (toId: String) -> (callerParams: a) -> (calleeParams: b) -> (args: c) -> (pos: d) -> (origins: e) -> f
totCallSiteGraphCross fromId toId callerParams calleeParams args pos origins =
  let edges = totCallSiteGraphGo callerParams calleeParams args pos origins []
  { from = fromId, to = toId, edges = edges }


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- C. The walk — COLLECT every self-call's size-change graph (a `List Graph`),
-- threading the same (scrut, origins, pos) context slice A's walk threaded. The
-- monoid is list concatenation (`totConcat`), not boolean disjunction; the tree
-- walk, shadowing, guard-narrowing, and origin-tracking are otherwise the SAME.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "tot: concat (graph lists)"
@description "Append every element of `xs` to `ys`. Order is irrelevant (the result feeds a deduped graph-SET closure), so a fold of appendItem suffices. Used to combine the self-call graphs collected from sub-expressions."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totConcat : (xs: a) -> (ys: b) -> b
totConcat xs ys =
  case head xs of
    Nothing -> ys
    Just x ->
      let ys2 = appendItem x ys
      case tail xs of
        Nothing -> ys2
        Just rest -> totConcat rest ys2

@label "tot: group lookup"
@description "The callee param-list of function `id` within the group (a `List {id, params, body}`), or Nothing when `id` is not a group member (a call OUTSIDE the mutually-recursive set — contributes no graph, sound: a missing edge only weakens the criterion). Maybe-returning (the totLookupOrigin shape) so callers pattern-match. Folds over the group comparing member.id == id."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totGroupLookup : (id: String) -> (group: a) -> Maybe b
totGroupLookup id group =
  case head group of
    Nothing -> Nothing
    Just member ->
      if eq member.id id
        then Just member.params
        else
          case tail group of
            Nothing -> Nothing
            Just rest -> totGroupLookup id rest

@label "tot: head may name a member"
@description "True when a call head or variable spelling may denote the function `id` (a canonical `module:name` id, or a bare id in hand-built groups). Stored bodies keep their source spellings while ids are canonical, so the match is spelling-normalized: a var-head call's `$dyn:` marker is stripped; the exact id matches; a dotted `Module.name` matches the id whose colons read as dots; a bare name matches every id whose code name it is (an over-approximation across modules: an extra match only adds a size-change graph or an escape, never removes one, so it can turn Total into Unknown but never the reverse). A colon spelling other than the exact id names something else."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totHeadMayName : (head: String) -> (id: String) -> Bool
totHeadMayName head id =
  let name = if startsWith head "$dyn:" then slice head 5 (length head) else head
  if eq name id then True
  else if contains name ":" then False
  else if contains name "." then eq name (join (split id ":") ".")
  else endsWith id (concat ":" name)

@label "tot: head names some member"
@description "True when the spelling may denote at least one member of the group (totHeadMayName)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totHeadNamesMember : (group: a) -> (head: String) -> Bool
totHeadNamesMember group head =
  fold (\found member -> if found then True else totHeadMayName head member.id) False group

@label "tot: here graph (cross-function call)"
@description "The size-change graph(s) contributed by a call `f(args)` in `fromId`'s body (slice C): ONE cross-function graph `fromId → m` for EVERY group member `m` the head may denote (totHeadMayName — canonical, dotted, bare and var-head spellings of the same function all count; built by totCallSiteGraphCross pairing the caller's params against m's params via the per-position oracle); a head naming no member contributes no graph. The graph's `to` is the member's canonical id, so composition meets at member ids whatever the call spelling. Generalizes slice B's `if eq f selfId` self-call check to a call to ANY member of the mutually-recursive set."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totHereGraph : (group: a) -> (fromId: String) -> (fromParams: b) -> (f: String) -> (args: c) -> (pos: d) -> (origins: e) -> g
totHereGraph group fromId fromParams f args pos origins =
  fold
    (\graphs member ->
      if totHeadMayName f member.id
        then appendItem (totCallSiteGraphCross fromId member.id fromParams member.params args pos origins) graphs
        else graphs)
    []
    group

@label "tot: collect graphs in arg list"
@description "Fold totCollectGraphs over a list of argument/child expressions, concatenating the call-site graphs found in each."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totGraphsInList : (group: g) -> (fromId: String) -> (fromParams: a) -> (scrut: a) -> (origins: a) -> (pos: a) -> (args: a) -> b
totGraphsInList group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos args =
  case head args of
    Nothing -> []
    Just a ->
      let these = totCollectGraphs group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos a
      case tail args of
        Nothing -> these
        Just rest -> totConcat these (totGraphsInList group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos rest)

@label "tot: collect graphs in record fields"
@description "Fold totCollectGraphs over a record's field values ({name, value} records), concatenating the call-site graphs found in each field value."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totGraphsInFields : (group: g) -> (fromId: String) -> (fromParams: a) -> (scrut: a) -> (origins: a) -> (pos: a) -> (fields: a) -> b
totGraphsInFields group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos fields =
  case head fields of
    Nothing -> []
    Just f ->
      let these = totCollectGraphs group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos f.value
      case tail fields of
        Nothing -> these
        Just rest -> totConcat these (totGraphsInFields group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos rest)

@label "tot: shadow source params"
@description "The caller's source-param list with every name in `binders` replaced by a `$shadowed:` spelling no variable can have. A binder (lambda param, arm pattern variable) that re-uses a source param's name hides that param for the binder's scope: an argument `EVar n` or `sub n 1` there denotes the BINDER, so the size-change oracle must not read it as the source param `n` (2026-10-03: `loop n` whose body applies a lambda that rebinds `n` and recurses on `n - 1` read Total). Renaming the hidden source slot removes every edge out of it in that scope (RelEq and measure edges compare names; a structural edge whose smaller variable was bound outside the scope is lost too — an under-approximation, never a false edge)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totShadowParams : (binders: a) -> (fromParams: b) -> b
totShadowParams binders fromParams =
  map (\p -> if elem p binders then concat "$shadowed:" p else p) fromParams

@label "tot: collect graphs in match arms"
@description "Per match arm, extend the (scrut, origins, pos) sets exactly as slice A/B's walk did — remove the arm pattern's bound vars from all three (shadowing), then add its constructor-bound (smaller) vars to scrut and to origins WITH their root param (= totRootOrigin of the scrutinee) IF the scrutinee is destructurable (NOT to pos) — and collect the call-site graphs of the arm guard (when present: a guard runs before the body, so a call in it is an executable edge too) and of the arm body. Concatenate across arms."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totGraphsInArms : (group: g) -> (fromId: String) -> (fromParams: a) -> (scrut: a) -> (origins: a) -> (pos: a) -> (s: Expr) -> (arms: a) -> b
totGraphsInArms group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos s arms =
  case head arms of
    Nothing -> []
    Just arm ->
      let canDestr = totScrutDecreasable scrut s
      let allVars = totCollectAllVars arm.pattern []
      let ctorVars = if canDestr then totCollectCtorVars arm.pattern [] else []
      let root = totRootOrigin s origins
      let scrut1 = totAppendAll ctorVars (totRemoveAll allVars scrut)
      let origins1 = totOriginsAddCtor ctorVars root (totOriginsRemoveAll allVars origins)
      let pos1 = totFactsForget allVars pos
      let fromParams1 = totShadowParams allVars fromParams
      let guardGraphs = case lookup arm "guard" of
        Nothing -> []
        Just guard -> totCollectGraphs group fromId fromParams1 scrut1 origins1 pos1 guard
      let these = totConcat guardGraphs (totCollectGraphs group fromId fromParams1 scrut1 origins1 pos1 arm.body)
      case tail arms of
        Nothing -> these
        Just rest -> totConcat these (totGraphsInArms group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos s rest)

@label "tot: collect graphs at a uniform call"
@description "The non-`if` ECall arm (slice C): when `f` is a group member the call contributes ITS cross-function call-site size-change graph (totHereGraph → totCallSiteGraphCross pairs the caller's params against the callee's via the per-position oracle); then recurse into every argument (a call nested in an argument is still collected). Replaces slice B's `eq f selfId` self-call test with the group lookup — a call to ANY member contributes its cross graph; non-members contribute nothing. Factored so the `if` guard-entry falls back here for short-arg `if`s."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totGraphsUniform : (group: g) -> (fromId: String) -> (fromParams: a) -> (scrut: a) -> (origins: a) -> (pos: a) -> (f: String) -> (args: a) -> b
totGraphsUniform group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos f args =
  let here = totHereGraph group fromId fromParams f args pos origins
  totConcat here (totGraphsInList group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos args)

@label "tot: collect graphs in if guard-entry"
@description "The `ECall \"if\"` guard entry (rung-2 narrowing, unchanged in shape): split the three args — collect from `cond` with the current `pos`, from `then` with `pos` extended by totPosFromCond cond (true-branch positivity), from `else` with totPosFromCondNeg cond (false-branch positivity) — and concatenate. An `if` with fewer than three args falls back to the uniform collection."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totGraphsInIf : (group: g) -> (fromId: String) -> (fromParams: a) -> (scrut: a) -> (origins: a) -> (pos: a) -> (f: String) -> (args: a) -> b
totGraphsInIf group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos f args =
  case head args of
    Nothing -> totGraphsUniform group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos f args
    Just cond ->
      case tail args of
        Nothing -> totGraphsUniform group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos f args
        Just rest1 ->
          case head rest1 of
            Nothing -> totGraphsUniform group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos f args
            Just thenE ->
              case tail rest1 of
                Nothing -> totGraphsUniform group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos f args
                Just rest2 ->
                  case head rest2 of
                    Nothing -> totGraphsUniform group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos f args
                    Just elseE ->
                      let gCond = totCollectGraphs group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos cond
                      let posT = totPosFromCond cond pos
                      let posE = totPosFromCondNeg cond pos
                      let gThen = totCollectGraphs group fromId fromParams scrut origins posT thenE
                      let gElse = totCollectGraphs group fromId fromParams scrut origins posE elseE
                      totConcat gCond (totConcat gThen gElse)

@label "tot: list literal call"
@description "True when a core ECall is the synthetic `appendItem` of a list literal (`[a, b]` lowers to an `appendItem` chain marked `lit = true`, the mark desugar keeps). The evaluator builds a literal natively; it never calls std:appendItem, so the walk treats it as a construction: its elements are walked, its head is no call."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totIsListLiteral : (e: Expr) -> Bool
totIsListLiteral e =
  case lookup e "lit" of
    Nothing -> False
    Just mark -> eq mark True

@label "tot: collect call-site graphs"
@description "The core totality walk over the 7-case core Expr, COLLECTING the size-change graph of every call to a GROUP member (slice C) in the subtree as a `List Graph`, given the current scrut/origins/pos sets and the caller (fromId, fromParams). ELit/EVar ⇒ no graphs; ECall `if` ⇒ the guard-entry (per-branch pos narrowing), other ECall ⇒ uniform (a call to a group member contributes its cross-function graph, then recurse args); ELambda removes its params from all three sets (shadowing); EMatch threads per-arm via totGraphsInArms (ctor-vars get their scrutinee's root origin); EConstruct/ERecord recurse into args/field-values. The SCT criterion is a GLOBAL decision over the closure of ALL call-graph graphs, so the walk collects, then checkMutualTotality decides once. Generalizes slice B's single-`selfId` walk (the one-object special case)."
@tags "engine" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
totCollectGraphs : (group: g) -> (fromId: String) -> (fromParams: a) -> (scrut: a) -> (origins: a) -> (pos: a) -> (e: Expr) -> b
totCollectGraphs group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos e =
  case e of
    ELit { value = _ } -> []
    EVar { name = _ } -> []
    ECall { fnId = f, args = args } ->
      if and (eq f "if") (not (eq (lookup e "structural") (Just false)))
        then totGraphsInIf group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos f args
        else if totIsListLiteral e
          then totGraphsInList group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos args
          else totGraphsUniform group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos f args
    ELambda { params = ps, body = bd } ->
      let scrut2 = totRemoveAll ps scrut
      let origins2 = totOriginsRemoveAll ps origins
      let pos2 = totFactsForget ps pos
      totCollectGraphs group fromId (totShadowParams ps fromParams) scrut2 origins2 pos2 bd
    EMatch { scrutinee = s, arms = arms } ->
      totConcat (totCollectGraphs group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos s) (totGraphsInArms group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos s arms)
    EConstruct { args = args } -> totGraphsInList group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos args
    ERecord { fields = fields } -> totGraphsInFields group fromId fromParams scrut origins pos fields

@label "tot: collect graphs from all group members"
@description "Seed S₀ of the call-graph closure: fold over every group member, collecting that member's call-site graphs with THAT member as the caller (fromId = m.id, fromParams = m.params, scrut seeded = its params, origins/pos empty). Concatenate across members. The result is every cross-function (and self) size-change graph in the whole mutually-recursive group's bodies."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totCollectAllMembers : (group: a) -> (members: b) -> c
totCollectAllMembers group members =
  case head members of
    Nothing -> []
    Just m ->
      let these = totCollectGraphs group m.id m.params m.params [] [] m.body
      case tail members of
        Nothing -> these
        Just rest -> totConcat these (totCollectAllMembers group rest)


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- D. The SCT decision — composition, the fuel-bounded closure fixpoint, and the
-- idempotent-strict-self-edge criterion.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "tot: add composed edge"
@description "Compose two edges that meet at an intermediate (e1.tgt == e2.src): the composed edge runs src e1 → tgt e2, strict iff EITHER is strict (totOr), inserted strict-dominantly. Helper for totComposeMatch."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totAddComposedEdge : (e1: a) -> (e2: a) -> (acc: b) -> b
totAddComposedEdge e1 e2 acc =
  let e = { src = e1.src, tgt = e2.tgt, strict = totOr e1.strict e2.strict }
  totAddStrongEdge e acc

@label "tot: compose-match"
@description "Add the composition of e1 and e2 to the accumulator IFF they meet (e1.tgt == e2.src); else leave the accumulator unchanged."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totComposeMatch : (e1: a) -> (e2: a) -> (acc: b) -> b
totComposeMatch e1 e2 acc =
  if eq e1.tgt e2.src then totAddComposedEdge e1 e2 acc else acc

@label "tot: compose inner (one e1 over h)"
@description "Fold one edge e1 of G against every edge of H, adding each meeting composition. Inner loop of graph composition."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totComposeInner : (e1: a) -> (h: b) -> (acc: c) -> c
totComposeInner e1 h acc =
  case head h of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just e2 ->
      let acc2 = totComposeMatch e1 e2 acc
      case tail h of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> totComposeInner e1 rest acc2

@label "tot: compose outer (G over H)"
@description "Fold every edge of G as e1 against H (via totComposeInner), accumulating the composed graph. Outer loop of graph composition."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totComposeOuter : (g: a) -> (h: b) -> (acc: c) -> c
totComposeOuter g h acc =
  case head g of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just e1 ->
      let acc2 = totComposeInner e1 h acc
      case tail g of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> totComposeOuter rest h acc2

@label "tot: compose graphs"
@description "Graph composition `G ; H` (slice C, PARTIAL — the caller guards G.to == H.from): the morphism `from = G.from, to = H.to`, with edges = for every pair (x → y ∈ G.edges, y → z ∈ H.edges) that meet, the edge x → z, strict iff either step is strict (strict-dominance on collisions). Models the size relation after two consecutive calls through the matching intermediate function. The edge fold (totComposeOuter/Inner/Match/totAddComposedEdge) is REUSED verbatim over the edge lists. Edges built via `let` then the literal (the inline-record-in-arg surprise)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totCompose : (g: a) -> (h: b) -> c
totCompose g h =
  let edges = totComposeOuter g.edges h.edges []
  { from = g.from, to = h.to, edges = edges }

@label "tot: maybe-add a composition (composable)"
@description "Compose graphs g and h (precondition g.to == h.from already checked); append the result to the accumulator set only if not already present (by graph set-equality). The deduped one-round expansion step for a composable pair."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totCompMaybeAdd2 : (g: a) -> (h: b) -> (acc: c) -> c
totCompMaybeAdd2 g h acc =
  let c = totCompose g h
  if totGraphMember c acc then acc else appendItem c acc

@label "tot: maybe-add a composition"
@description "Slice C: composition is a PARTIAL operation — defined only when the intermediate function matches (g.to == h.from). When they match, compose + dedup-add (totCompMaybeAdd2); when they don't, SKIP the pair entirely (NO graph added — NOT an empty graph, which would pollute the closure with a spurious idempotent). This guard is what keeps the call graph's composition a category morphism restricted to matching intermediates."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totCompMaybeAdd : (g: a) -> (h: b) -> (acc: c) -> c
totCompMaybeAdd g h acc =
  if eq g.to h.from then totCompMaybeAdd2 g h acc else acc

@label "tot: compositions inner (g over all)"
@description "Fold graph g against every graph in `hs`, maybe-adding each composition g ; h to the accumulator set. Inner loop of one closure round."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totCompInner : (g: a) -> (hs: b) -> (acc: c) -> c
totCompInner g hs acc =
  case head hs of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just h ->
      let acc2 = totCompMaybeAdd g h acc
      case tail hs of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> totCompInner g rest acc2

@label "tot: compositions outer"
@description "Fold every graph of `gs` as the left operand against the full graph list `allG` (via totCompInner), accumulating into the set. Outer loop of one closure round."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totCompOuter : (allG: a) -> (gs: b) -> (acc: c) -> c
totCompOuter allG gs acc =
  case head gs of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just g ->
      let acc2 = totCompInner g allG acc
      case tail gs of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> totCompOuter allG rest acc2

@label "tot: one closure round"
@description "One round of the closure: `graphs` plus normalize(G ; H) for every ordered pair (G, H) of graphs, each inserted only if not already present (deduped by set-equality). Seeds the accumulator with `graphs` itself, so the round is non-shrinking (next ⊇ graphs)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totAddCompositions : (graphs: a) -> b
totAddCompositions graphs = totCompOuter graphs graphs graphs

@label "tot: closure step"
@description "One fuel-bounded fixpoint step: compute the next round; if it added nothing (set-equal to the current graphs) return Just graphs (fixpoint reached), else recurse with one less fuel on the expanded set. Helper for totClose (keeps the fuel guard a single-line if)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totCloseStep : (fuel: a) -> (graphs: b) -> Maybe b
totCloseStep fuel graphs =
  let next = totAddCompositions graphs
  if totGraphSetEq next graphs then Just graphs else totClose (sub fuel 1) next

@label "tot: closure (fuel-bounded fixpoint)"
@description "The transitive closure of the graph set under composition, fuel-bounded: Nothing when fuel is exhausted (a SOUND under-approximation — the caller maps Nothing → Unknown; we NEVER check a partial closure for Total), else the fixpoint (totCloseStep) reached when a round adds no new graph. Structurally recursive on `fuel` (the structural-decreasing measure). The closure is finite (≤ 3^(n²) graphs over n params); fuel 256 is a generous pathological backstop — real code saturates in a handful of rounds via the early no-change exit. Tunable."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totClose : (fuel: a) -> (graphs: b) -> Maybe b
totClose fuel graphs =
  if eq fuel 0 then Nothing else totCloseStep fuel graphs

@label "tot: idempotent edge-set check"
@description "Helper for totIsIdempotent (slice C): given a graph g whose from == to is already established, True when composing g with itself leaves its edge set unchanged ((g ; g).edges == g.edges, by edge set-equality). Kept separate to avoid a let-in-then-branch."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totIsIdempotentEdges : (g: a) -> Bool
totIsIdempotentEdges g =
  let c = totCompose g g
  totEdgesEq c.edges g.edges

@label "tot: graph is idempotent"
@description "True when graph `g` is idempotent under composition (`g ; g = g`). Slice C: an idempotent graph is NECESSARILY a same-function cycle, so the from == to precondition is checked FIRST (a g with from ≠ to could not equal g ; g, whose from = g.from but whose composition only meets if g.to == g.from); then the edge set must be fixed. An idempotent graph describes a stable infinite call path returning to its function — the graphs the SCT criterion imposes a descent obligation on."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totIsIdempotent : (g: a) -> Bool
totIsIdempotent g = if eq g.from g.to then totIsIdempotentEdges g else False

@label "tot: graph has strict self-edge"
@description "True when the edge-list `edges` has a strictly-descending SELF-edge (∃ edge with src == tgt AND strict). The descent witness an idempotent graph must carry for SCT. Called on `g.edges` of an idempotent graph (whose from == to, so a src==tgt edge is a true self-loop on a single parameter)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totHasStrictDiagonal : (edges: a) -> Bool
totHasStrictDiagonal edges =
  case head edges of
    Nothing -> False
    Just e ->
      let thisDiag = if eq e.src e.tgt then e.strict else False
      case tail edges of
        Nothing -> thisDiag
        Just rest -> totOr thisDiag (totHasStrictDiagonal rest)

@label "tot: all idempotents descend"
@description "Fold the closure: every IDEMPOTENT graph must have a strictly-descending self-edge; a non-idempotent graph imposes no obligation (True). All obligations must hold (the SCT criterion). Slice C: the idempotent graphs are the `f → f` cycles of the call graph; each must strictly descend some parameter."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totAllIdempotentsDescend : (graphs: a) -> Bool
totAllIdempotentsDescend graphs =
  case head graphs of
    Nothing -> True
    Just g ->
      let thisOk = if totIsIdempotent g then totHasStrictDiagonal g.edges else True
      case tail graphs of
        Nothing -> thisOk
        Just rest -> totAnd thisOk (totAllIdempotentsDescend rest)

@label "tot: SCT decide (over a non-empty graph set)"
@description "Run the closure and apply the SCT criterion: fuel exhaustion (Nothing) ⇒ False (a sound Unknown), else every idempotent in the closure must strictly descend."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totSctDecide : (graphs: a) -> Bool
totSctDecide graphs =
  case totClose 256 graphs of
    Nothing -> False
    Just closure -> totAllIdempotentsDescend closure

@label "tot: is empty list"
@description "True when the list is empty (no head). Drives the no-self-call ⇒ vacuously total fast path."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3d"
@category "engine-internal"
totIsEmptyList : (xs: a) -> Bool
totIsEmptyList xs =
  case head xs of
    Nothing -> True
    Just _ -> False

@label "tot: SCT terminating"
@description "The size-change termination decision for a function GROUP (slice C): no call-graph graph at all (empty set) ⇒ vacuously total; else the closure-based SCT criterion (every idempotent `f → f` graph in the transitive closure under restricted composition has a strictly-descending self-edge; fuel exhaustion ⇒ False/Unknown). The single-function case is the one-object special case (every graph is `f → f`)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
@category "engine-internal"
totSctTerminating : (graphs: a) -> Bool
totSctTerminating graphs =
  if totIsEmptyList graphs then True else totSctDecide graphs


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- E. The unchecked-reference audit (2026-10-02). The size-change walk above
-- sees only CALLS to group members. Two other executable routes back into a
-- group are invisible to it, and either one beside a visibly decreasing call
-- would yield a false Total: a member taken as a VALUE (`map f xs` — whoever
-- receives it can call it with any argument), and a var-head call to a name no
-- enclosing binder binds and no member is (a local recursive `where` binding
-- lowers to exactly that: `$ (\go -> go n) (\k -> go k)` — the inner `go` is
-- free). The audit walks every member body with its lexical binders (the
-- member's params, lambda params, arm pattern vars) and refuses both.
--
-- A THIRD route (2026-10-03): INVOKING a callable the walk cannot see the body
-- of. A var-head call `$dyn:k` or an apply `k $ x` whose callee is a function
-- parameter, an arm pattern variable, a lambda parameter, or a field of one
-- (`r.f`), or an apply whose callee is any other computed expression, runs code
-- the size-change graphs never saw: a callback that re-enters the group
-- (`unroll r = case r of Roll k -> k r` with `start = unroll (Roll unroll)`), a
-- self-application, a stored function. Such an invocation is refused. The one
-- precise acceptance is a CHECKED LOCAL CLOSURE: a name bound by an immediately
-- applied lambda (the `let` / `where` lowering `$ (\g -> body) (\k -> …)`) to a
-- lambda literal, invoked by its own name in the scope of that binding. Its body
-- is the literal argument, which this audit and the size-change walk both walk
-- in place, and a non-recursive `let` cannot make it refer to itself.
--
-- A FOURTH route (2026-10-03): OVER-APPLICATION. The evaluator binds a callee's
-- params, evaluates its body and, when arguments are left over and the result
-- is callable, applies the leftovers to that result (json-logic.ts, the
-- eta-reduction spill). So `idf p r` with `idf y = y` invokes p, and `g f x` with
-- `g = \k -> k` invokes f: an invocation of a value the walk never checked.
-- Refused here: a call to a group member, a lambda literal, or a checked local
-- closure with more arguments than its params (a closure remembers the arity
-- of its literal). Over-application of a registry function outside the group
-- is refused by the kernel-gate entry (verdictTagForIn), which knows its params.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "tot: spelling root"
@description "The lexical root of a variable or var-head spelling: the text before the first dot (`row` for `row.args`), with a var-head call's `$dyn:` marker stripped. A spelling whose root a binder binds is a local value or a field of one."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totSpellingRoot : (name: String) -> String
totSpellingRoot name =
  let local = if startsWith name "$dyn:" then slice name 5 (length name) else name
  fromMaybe local (head (split local "."))

@label "tot: closure over-applied"
@description "For a local callee spelled exactly `name`: True unless `closures` (checked local closures, {name, arity} records, the innermost first) holds `name` with an arity of at least `argc`. A bound name that is no checked closure is a callback (True); a checked closure applied to more arguments than its lambda literal has params spills the rest onto its result (True)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totClosureOverApplied : (closures: a) -> (name: String) -> (argc: Number) -> Bool
totClosureOverApplied closures name argc =
  let found = fold (\state c -> if state.seen then state else if eq c.name name then { seen = True, unchecked = gt argc c.arity } else state) { seen = False, unchecked = True } closures
  found.unchecked

@label "tot: member over-applied"
@description "True when the spelling may denote a group member (totHeadMayName) whose params are fewer than `argc`: the call spills the extra arguments onto the member's result, an invocation the size-change graphs do not see."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totMemberOverApplied : (group: a) -> (name: String) -> (argc: Number) -> Bool
totMemberOverApplied group name argc =
  fold (\found member -> if found then True else and (totHeadMayName name member.id) (gt argc (length member.params))) False group

@label "tot: remove closures"
@description "Drop every checked local closure whose name is in `names` (a binder that shadows it)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totRemoveClosures : (names: a) -> (closures: b) -> b
totRemoveClosures names closures =
  filter (\c -> not (elem c.name names)) closures

@label "tot: unchecked invocation of a named callable"
@description "True when invoking the callable spelled `name` with `argc` arguments (a var-head call's name with `$dyn:` stripped, or the variable an apply `$` calls) is a route the size-change walk cannot check. A name whose root an enclosing binder binds is a local: accepted only when it is exactly a checked local closure applied to at most its arity (totClosureOverApplied; not a field read of one); any other local (a parameter, a pattern variable, a field of either) is a callback whose body is never seen. An unbound name is accepted when `memberCallOk` and it may denote a group member applied to at most its params (a var-head call to a member has its size-change graph; totMemberOverApplied); when not `memberCallOk` (an apply `$`, which builds no graph), naming a member is refused and naming anything else is taken as a call outside the group: that such a name denotes a gathered registry function is checked by the kernel-gate entry (verdictTagForIn, anaAppliesUnresolved), not here — a group-only caller (the census, inference trust) must discharge it itself. An unbound var-head name that names no member is an unresolvable dynamic call (a local recursive binding lowers to one)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totUncheckedInvoke : (group: a) -> (bound: b) -> (closures: c) -> (name: String) -> (argc: Number) -> (memberCallOk: Bool) -> Bool
totUncheckedInvoke group bound closures name argc memberCallOk =
  let root = totSpellingRoot name
  if elem root bound then (if eq name root then totClosureOverApplied closures name argc else True)
  else if memberCallOk then (if totHeadNamesMember group name then totMemberOverApplied group name argc else True)
  else totHeadNamesMember group name

@label "tot: lambda-literal argument closures"
@description "The checked local closures an immediately applied lambda binds: for each param whose positional argument is itself a lambda literal, the record {name, arity} (the param, and the literal's param count). The applied body sees that name bound to a closure whose body is the literal (the `let` / `where` lowering binds one name per application)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totLambdaArgClosures : (params: a) -> (args: b) -> c
totLambdaArgClosures params args =
  case head params of
    Nothing -> []
    Just p ->
      case head args of
        Nothing -> []
        Just arg ->
          let rest = totLambdaArgClosures (totTail params) (totTail args)
          case arg of
            ELambda { params = lps } -> appendItem { name = p, arity = length lps } rest
            _ -> rest

@label "tot: unchecked reference in a list"
@description "True when any expression of the list holds an unchecked route (totUncheckedReference) under the same binders and closures."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totUncheckedInList : (group: a) -> (bound: b) -> (closures: c) -> (es: d) -> Bool
totUncheckedInList group bound closures es =
  fold (\found a -> if found then True else totUncheckedReference group bound closures a) False es

@label "tot: unchecked apply"
@description "The apply form `$ callee args…`. An immediately applied lambda (the `let` / `where` / `do` lowering) walks its arguments in the current scope, then its body with the lambda params bound, each param whose argument is a lambda literal becoming a checked local closure (with the literal's arity) and every other param shadowing any closure of that name; applied to more arguments than it has params, it spills the rest onto its result and is refused. A variable callee is an invocation judged by totUncheckedInvoke with the argument count (no member graph: `$` builds none). Any other callee (a call result, a match, a construction) is a computed callable and is refused."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totUncheckedApply : (group: a) -> (bound: b) -> (closures: c) -> (args: d) -> Bool
totUncheckedApply group bound closures args =
  case head args of
    Nothing -> False
    Just callee ->
      let rest = totTail args
      case callee of
        ELambda { params = ps, body = bd } ->
          if gt (length rest) (length ps) then True
          else if totUncheckedInList group bound closures rest then True
          else totUncheckedReference group (totAppendAll ps bound) (totConcat (totLambdaArgClosures ps rest) (totRemoveClosures ps closures)) bd
        EVar { name = n } ->
          if totUncheckedInvoke group bound closures n (length rest) False then True
          else totUncheckedInList group bound closures rest
        _ -> True

@label "tot: unchecked reference"
@description "True when the core Expr `e`, under the lexical binders `bound` and the checked local closures `closures`, holds an executable route into the group that the size-change walk cannot check: an EVar whose root is unbound and which may denote a member (totHeadNamesMember — the member escapes as a value); a `$dyn:` var-head call the walk cannot check (totUncheckedInvoke: a callable parameter, pattern variable or field invoked, an unbound name that is no member — e.g. a local recursive binding — or a closure or member over-applied); an apply `$` whose callee is not a checked closure or a lambda literal, or that over-applies one (totUncheckedApply); a string-head call that over-applies a group member (totMemberOverApplied; a list literal's synthetic appendItem excepted). Lambda params and arm pattern vars extend `bound` and shadow `closures` for their bodies; arm guards are walked like bodies. Any extra binder only removes a refusal for a genuinely local name, and the member match over-approximates, so the audit can only turn Total into Unknown."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totUncheckedReference : (group: a) -> (bound: b) -> (closures: c) -> (e: Expr) -> Bool
totUncheckedReference group bound closures e =
  case e of
    ELit { value = _ } -> False
    EVar { name = n } -> if elem (totSpellingRoot n) bound then False else totHeadNamesMember group n
    ECall { fnId = f, args = args } ->
      if startsWith f "$dyn:" then
        (if totUncheckedInvoke group bound closures (slice f 5 (length f)) (length args) True then True
         else totUncheckedInList group bound closures args)
      else if eq f "$" then totUncheckedApply group bound closures args
      else if totIsListLiteral e then totUncheckedInList group bound closures args
      else if totMemberOverApplied group f (length args) then True
      else totUncheckedInList group bound closures args
    ELambda { params = ps, body = bd } -> totUncheckedReference group (totAppendAll ps bound) (totRemoveClosures ps closures) bd
    EMatch { scrutinee = s, arms = arms } ->
      if totUncheckedReference group bound closures s then True
      else
        fold
          (\found arm ->
            if found then True
            else
              let armVars = totCollectAllVars arm.pattern []
              let armBound = totAppendAll armVars bound
              let armClosures = totRemoveClosures armVars closures
              case lookup arm "guard" of
                Nothing -> totUncheckedReference group armBound armClosures arm.body
                Just guard ->
                  if totUncheckedReference group armBound armClosures guard then True
                  else totUncheckedReference group armBound armClosures arm.body)
          False
          arms
    EConstruct { args = args } -> totUncheckedInList group bound closures args
    ERecord { fields = fields } -> fold (\found field -> if found then True else totUncheckedReference group bound closures field.value) False fields

@label "tot: group has an unchecked reference"
@description "True when any member body, under its own params (and no closures), holds an unchecked route into the group (totUncheckedReference)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "totality" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
totGroupUnchecked : (group: a) -> Bool
totGroupUnchecked group =
  fold (\found member -> if found then True else totUncheckedReference group member.params [] member.body) False group


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- checkMutualTotality — the rung-3c entry (slice C): the MUTUAL-recursion
-- size-change decision over a SET of functions. `group` is a `List {id, params,
-- body}` — the mutually-recursive set the caller supplies (the SCC; slice C does
-- NOT discover the SCCs itself — D-3e-4). Seed S₀ = every call-site graph from
-- EVERY member's body (totCollectAllMembers), then apply the call-graph SCT
-- criterion (totSctTerminating): `Total` when every IDEMPOTENT `f → f` graph in
-- the closure under restricted composition strictly descends (or no call-graph
-- graph exists at all); else `Unknown`. A singleton group = the single-function
-- case (slice B), so checkStructuralTotality below is sugar over this.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "Check mutual-recursion totality (rung 3c)"
@description "Rung-3c MUTUAL-recursion totality check over a function GROUP (a `List {id, params, body}` of the mutually-recursive set). Generalizes the single-function size-change closure (slice B) to a CALL GRAPH over a set of functions (Lee–Jones–Ben-Amram general form): each call site `fₐ → fᵦ` yields a size-change graph `{from = fₐ, to = fᵦ, edges}` whose edges run from the caller's params to the callee's param-slots (the per-position oracle totPosIsLt/totPosIsEq reused verbatim); composition `G ; H` is defined ONLY when G.to == H.from (matching intermediate function); the fuel-bounded transitive closure is taken; the program is size-change terminating iff every IDEMPOTENT graph (`from == to` AND `g ; g = g`, necessarily an `f → f` cycle) has a strictly-descending self-edge. Returns Total when the group is size-change terminating (incl. the structural mutual win `f x = …g t…` / `g y = …f t…`, the measure mutual win, the 3-function cycle whose `f → f` idempotent surfaces only at closure depth 3), or there is no call-graph graph at all; Unknown when some idempotent `f → f` graph has no strict self-edge (the mutual non-termination canaries `f a = g a` / `g b = f b`, the permutation ping-pong), or the closure exceeded the fuel bound, or for the inherited fences (`≠ 0`/ℕ-typed equality guards need a type — `== 0`-guarded even/odd stays Unknown; k ≥ 2 / non-`sub` measures). SOUND: every edge asserts a relation the per-position oracle proved; composition only derives relations holding along call-graph paths; a missing edge (a call outside the group, an unrecognized shape) only weakens the criterion ⇒ Unknown, never a wrong Total. A passed group that is not mutually closed loses edges (sound). A missing GRAPH is different from a missing edge: a call site the walk fails to recognise removes an obligation and could fake Total, so call heads match members by spelling (totHeadMayName: canonical, dotted, bare and var-head spellings), and a member taken as a value or a var-head call to an unbound non-member name refuses first (totGroupUnchecked ⇒ Unknown; 2026-10-02). Never returns Partial — the @partial escape-hatch is folded by totalityVerdict."
@tags "engine" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
checkMutualTotality : (group: a) -> Totality
checkMutualTotality group =
  if totGroupUnchecked group
    then Unknown { reason = "a group member is taken as a value, or a var-head call names nothing a binder or the group provides (e.g. a local recursive binding): the size-change graphs cannot check that route" }
    else
      let graphs = totCollectAllMembers group group
      if totSctTerminating graphs
        then Total
        else Unknown { reason = "rung-3c: the mutual-recursion call graph is not size-change terminating — some idempotent f→f graph in the closure has no strictly-descending self-edge (or the closure exceeded the fuel bound); a type-guarded (≠0 on ℕ) or outside-the-abstraction argument may still hold" }


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- checkStructuralTotality — the rung-1/2/3a/3b SINGLE-FUNCTION entry, now
-- SINGLETON SUGAR over checkMutualTotality (slice C, D-3e-2): a single function
-- is the one-object special case of the call graph (every graph is `f → f`, every
-- composition is defined, the from == to guard is always true), so the closure +
-- criterion reduce EXACTLY to slice B's. The signature is unchanged (preserves the
-- 40 single-function tests + any consumer) — the regression guard.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "Check structural + measure + lexicographic + size-change totality (rung 1 + 2 + 3a + 3b)"
@description "Single-function totality check (rung 1 structural-recursion + rung 2 guarded measure + rung 3a lexicographic + rung 3b size-change graph closure) over a function's core Expr body. As of slice C (rung 3c) this is SINGLETON SUGAR over checkMutualTotality — the function becomes a one-member group `[{id = selfId, params, body}]`, so the mutual call-graph closure reduces to the single-function self-call closure (the one-object special case): Total iff the recursion is size-change terminating (every IDEMPOTENT graph in the transitive closure under composition has a strictly-descending self-edge), or there is no self-call. COMPLETE for the size-change abstraction: subsumes rungs 1+2+3a (structural / measure / lexicographic-identity descents) AND proves PERMUTED / reordering / multi-step-rotation descents for which no fixed parameter order works (`f a b = if a>0 then f b (a-1) else 0` ⇒ Total). SOUND throughout: every edge asserts a relation the per-position oracle proved, composition only derives two-call relations, a missing edge only makes the criterion harder (⇒ Unknown, never a wrong Total); the cross-position soundness repairs (`f (Cons h t) t`, `f (b+1) (a-1)`) stay Unknown (G = {a →↓ b}; G ; G = {} empty idempotent, no strict self-edge). Returns Unknown when the closure has a non-descending idempotent, or the fuel-bounded fixpoint is exhausted, or for the inherited fences (`≠ 0`/ℕ-typed guards need a type; k ≥ 2 / non-`sub` measures). Never returns Partial — folded by totalityVerdict. Sound: variable shadowing removes re-bound names from ALL of scrut/origins/pos."
@tags "engine" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3e"
checkStructuralTotality : (selfId: String) -> (params: a) -> (body: Expr) -> Totality
checkStructuralTotality selfId params body =
  let member = { id = selfId, params = params, body = body }
  checkMutualTotality (appendItem member [])


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- totalityVerdict — the three-valued producer: fold the `@partial` escape-
-- hatch in front of the rung-1 check. A declared-partial definition is
-- `Partial` (accepted-with-acknowledgement, excluded from proof paths);
-- otherwise the rung-1 verdict (`Total | Unknown`).
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "Totality verdict"
@description "The three-valued totality verdict for a definition: Partial when declared @partial (an acknowledged escape-hatch — hard-rejected on proof-carrying paths, accepted elsewhere), otherwise the rung-1 structural-recursion verdict (Total | Unknown). The gate consumer reads this: Partial is a hard-reject, Unknown a warning (a reject on proof-carrying paths), Total an accept."
@tags "engine" "totality" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-1"
totalityVerdict : (declaredPartial: Bool) -> (selfId: String) -> (params: a) -> (body: Expr) -> Totality
totalityVerdict declaredPartial selfId params body =
  if declaredPartial
    then Partial { reason = "declared partial (@partial escape-hatch)" }
    else checkStructuralTotality selfId params body
